1
00:00:53,375 --> 00:00:55,636
[narrator]
<i>At the center of the universe,</i>

2
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,854
<i>at the border between
the light and the dark</i>

3
00:00:57,898 --> 00:01:00,680
<i>stands Castle Grayskull.</i>

4
00:01:00,723 --> 00:01:03,420
<i>For countless ages,
the Sorceress of Grayskull</i>

5
00:01:03,463 --> 00:01:05,768
<i>has kept this universe
in harmony.</i>

6
00:01:05,812 --> 00:01:08,724
<i>But the armies
of darkness do not rest,</i>

7
00:01:08,768 --> 00:01:12,160
<i>and the capture of Grayskull
is ever most in their minds.</i>

8
00:01:12,203 --> 00:01:17,160
<i>For to those that control
Grayskull will come the power.</i>

9
00:01:17,203 --> 00:01:20,856
<i>The power to be supreme.
The power to be almighty.</i>

10
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:25,551
<i>The power to be
masters of the universe.</i>

11
00:01:25,595 --> 00:01:27,595
[theme music playing]

12
00:03:22,517 --> 00:03:24,822
[Skeletor]
Report, Evil-Lyn. Speak.

13
00:03:24,865 --> 00:03:26,996
[Evil-Lyn] We have sealed
the gates to the city.

14
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:30,909
The castle is secure and we are
closing in on the Thenurian as we speak.

15
00:03:30,952 --> 00:03:32,387
[Skeletor] Yes, yes.
And He-Man?

16
00:03:32,431 --> 00:03:34,648
[Evil-Lyn] He continues
to lead the resistance.

17
00:03:34,692 --> 00:03:37,431
I assure you, we will have
him before the day is out.

18
00:03:38,997 --> 00:03:42,345
[Skeletor] I want him
kneeling at my feet.

19
00:03:43,824 --> 00:03:45,432
After all this time,

20
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,954
- Grayskull is ours.
- No!

21
00:03:56,954 --> 00:03:58,520
Mine.

22
00:04:01,302 --> 00:04:02,912
[Sorceress]
The power of Grayskull

23
00:04:02,955 --> 00:04:04,912
- has not yet passed to you.
- [Skeletor] Hmm.

24
00:04:06,521 --> 00:04:08,737
Someone is speaking to me.

25
00:04:10,912 --> 00:04:14,000
Yes. Sorceress.

26
00:04:14,043 --> 00:04:16,174
My lovely prisoner.

27
00:04:16,217 --> 00:04:19,130
My prisoner at last.

28
00:04:21,043 --> 00:04:24,870
I've won. I've won.

29
00:04:24,914 --> 00:04:29,262
The darkness is rising
to embrace you.

30
00:04:29,304 --> 00:04:33,262
The dark can embrace
the light but never eclipse it.

31
00:04:33,305 --> 00:04:35,175
You have not won yet, Skeletor.

32
00:04:35,218 --> 00:04:36,957
He-Man is still alive.

33
00:04:37,001 --> 00:04:38,828
- I can feel it.
- Really?

34
00:04:39,697 --> 00:04:42,176
How sensitive you are.

35
00:04:42,219 --> 00:04:44,566
Can you feel this?

36
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:47,132
[Sorceress gasps]

37
00:04:47,176 --> 00:04:49,654
[moaning]

38
00:04:55,916 --> 00:04:58,438
Evil-Lyn,
activate the holosphere.

39
00:05:01,916 --> 00:05:06,394
People of Eternia,
the war is over.

40
00:05:06,438 --> 00:05:09,481
<i>My forces are victorious.</i>

41
00:05:09,525 --> 00:05:13,047
<i>The Sorceress of Grayskull
is my prisoner,</i>

42
00:05:13,091 --> 00:05:16,917
<i>and her powers
are now joined with mine.</i>

43
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:20,265
<i>Let this be my first decree.</i>

44
00:05:20,308 --> 00:05:24,222
<i>Those who do not
pledge themselves to me</i>

45
00:05:24,266 --> 00:05:27,657
<i>shall be destroyed.</i>

46
00:05:27,701 --> 00:05:30,832
<i>The new age begins.</i>

47
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:05,616
[grunts]

48
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,835
[both grunting]

49
00:06:22,183 --> 00:06:23,487
[weapons firing]

50
00:06:36,271 --> 00:06:38,358
He-Man, thank the Sorceress
you're alive.

51
00:06:38,401 --> 00:06:39,445
I've been looking for you.

52
00:06:45,185 --> 00:06:46,054
[Teela] Oh.

53
00:06:47,446 --> 00:06:49,185
Grayskull...

54
00:06:49,228 --> 00:06:51,794
- It was terrible.
- How many units are left?

55
00:06:51,838 --> 00:06:55,012
Not many. All of us
were scattered.

56
00:06:55,055 --> 00:06:57,576
Suddenly, they were everywhere.

57
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,750
- Chaos.
- Someone betrayed us.

58
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:02,447
[Gwildor] Help! Help!

59
00:07:02,490 --> 00:07:04,360
- Get me out of this!
- It's all right.

60
00:07:04,403 --> 00:07:09,969
Help! Help! Help, somebody.

61
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:12,448
- Help. - All right,
all right, we heard you.

62
00:07:12,491 --> 00:07:14,404
- Pull the pole out.
- [Gwildor] Careful. Careful.

63
00:07:14,448 --> 00:07:17,622
- [Man-at-Arms] Thank the Sorceress.
- I hear you come.

64
00:07:17,665 --> 00:07:21,318
Ah! Oh. Uh...

65
00:07:21,362 --> 00:07:23,362
[Man-at-Arms] Who are you?

66
00:07:23,405 --> 00:07:26,449
Why, I am Gwildor of Thenur,

67
00:07:26,492 --> 00:07:28,362
locksmith and inventor.

68
00:07:28,405 --> 00:07:31,405
Ah! Skeletor's forces
were hunting me down.

69
00:07:31,449 --> 00:07:34,623
A million blessings upon you
for saving my life.

70
00:07:34,666 --> 00:07:38,797
No blessing is necessary. Any
foe of Skeletor's is a friend of ours.

71
00:07:38,841 --> 00:07:40,450
Now, why are you
so important to Skeletor?

72
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,667
Uh... Help me.

73
00:07:43,711 --> 00:07:44,972
[grunting]

74
00:07:46,711 --> 00:07:47,972
[chuckles]

75
00:07:48,016 --> 00:07:50,667
I'd better show you.
Please come with me.

76
00:07:57,451 --> 00:08:00,799
I remember the days we
didn't have to lock our doors.

77
00:08:00,843 --> 00:08:03,755
Those days will
come back. Oh, yes.

78
00:08:06,973 --> 00:08:08,191
[lock whines and beeps]

79
00:08:12,105 --> 00:08:15,669
Enter, enter.

80
00:08:15,713 --> 00:08:18,496
Come on, come in.
Welcome to my home.

81
00:08:19,974 --> 00:08:21,279
Come on.

82
00:08:22,409 --> 00:08:23,757
Come, come, come.

83
00:08:33,584 --> 00:08:36,454
[mechanical whirring]

84
00:08:36,497 --> 00:08:41,628
[Gwildor clears throat] Now, you ask
why is Skeletor after me? Ha!

85
00:08:41,671 --> 00:08:43,628
Because of my invention.

86
00:08:45,455 --> 00:08:47,890
Because of this.

87
00:08:50,585 --> 00:08:52,672
Now I wish I hadn't created it.

88
00:08:52,716 --> 00:08:55,499
Skeletor wants me killed
so I can't make another one.

89
00:08:56,977 --> 00:09:00,021
If he knew
I had this prototype... Oh.

90
00:09:00,064 --> 00:09:01,412
What is it?

91
00:09:01,456 --> 00:09:02,848
What does it do?

92
00:09:05,022 --> 00:09:06,456
I call it

93
00:09:07,326 --> 00:09:09,065
the Cosmic Key.

94
00:09:13,978 --> 00:09:17,370
It is the most unique key
in the universe.

95
00:09:17,413 --> 00:09:19,631
The tones it generates

96
00:09:19,674 --> 00:09:22,587
can open a doorway to anywhere.

97
00:09:22,631 --> 00:09:25,327
- Anywhere?
- Exactly.

98
00:09:25,371 --> 00:09:27,850
One simply computes
gravitonic tones

99
00:09:27,893 --> 00:09:30,240
for a specific destination,

100
00:09:30,284 --> 00:09:32,285
activates the energizer and...

101
00:09:32,327 --> 00:09:35,675
And that's how Skeletor's troops
got into the city and surprised us.

102
00:09:37,589 --> 00:09:40,198
Yes. Yes.

103
00:09:41,938 --> 00:09:43,198
I'm afraid so.

104
00:09:44,068 --> 00:09:46,676
You little worm.

105
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:50,025
- Don't you realize what you've done?
- Easy, Teela. He didn't know.

106
00:09:50,068 --> 00:09:54,764
That's right. How could I know?
We Thenurians are a peaceful race.

107
00:09:54,808 --> 00:09:57,329
Trusting in every way.

108
00:09:57,373 --> 00:10:00,026
A woman came to see me.

109
00:10:00,069 --> 00:10:03,504
Said she heard about
my fame as a locksmith.

110
00:10:03,548 --> 00:10:07,461
She seemed, uh,
interested in my work.

111
00:10:07,504 --> 00:10:09,940
How could I know
she was from Snake Mountain?

112
00:10:09,983 --> 00:10:12,288
- She was beautiful.
- That would be Evil-Lyn.

113
00:10:12,331 --> 00:10:14,896
She tricked me.
She stole the key.

114
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,201
Gwildor,

115
00:10:16,244 --> 00:10:19,418
can this device of yours
get us to Grayskull?

116
00:10:19,462 --> 00:10:22,157
- Certainly.
- To the Sorceress?

117
00:10:22,201 --> 00:10:25,897
Those were the first coordinates
I calculated before she came.

118
00:10:25,941 --> 00:10:28,202
- [chuckles softly] Oh, good.
- Oh, but we can't. We can't.

119
00:10:28,245 --> 00:10:32,506
If we disturb the gravitonic
waves, Skeletor's key will locate us.

120
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:33,680
- [alarm sounding]
- [Gwildor] Oh.

121
00:10:33,724 --> 00:10:35,463
Sounds like he's
already located us.

122
00:10:36,942 --> 00:10:38,029
[Karg] Warlord, to the point.

123
00:10:41,898 --> 00:10:45,072
No, no, no. Not that way.
This way, the secret passage.

124
00:10:46,203 --> 00:10:49,246
- Hurry. Hurry.
- Go.

125
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:51,681
- In the corner, there. Let's move.
- [Teela] Right.

126
00:10:51,725 --> 00:10:53,725
Gwildor, where does this lead?

127
00:10:53,768 --> 00:10:55,943
To the caverns
underneath Grayskull.

128
00:10:55,986 --> 00:10:57,508
Ionize.

129
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,030
Gwildor, hurry.

130
00:11:00,073 --> 00:11:02,465
- [Gwildor] Yes, yes.
- [He-Man] Come on.

131
00:11:02,508 --> 00:11:04,987
I don't like adventures. Oh!

132
00:11:13,074 --> 00:11:14,509
[explodes]

133
00:11:16,248 --> 00:11:18,770
[Karg] Secure the room. Hurry.

134
00:11:21,945 --> 00:11:25,206
Find the key.
Tear this place apart.

135
00:11:35,207 --> 00:11:36,598
He-Man, we made it. Look.

136
00:11:36,642 --> 00:11:39,511
Shh, shh! I know he's here
waiting for us.

137
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:42,860
- You're right. It's too quiet.
- Look. The Sorceress.

138
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:44,816
Come on.

139
00:11:46,034 --> 00:11:47,469
Gwildor, hurry.

140
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:51,251
- [Man-at-Arms] Shh!
- [He-Man] Be careful.

141
00:11:51,295 --> 00:11:51,861
[Man-at-Arms] Quiet.

142
00:12:12,210 --> 00:12:13,123
Sorceress?

143
00:12:15,079 --> 00:12:16,645
Sorceress, we'll free you.

144
00:12:16,688 --> 00:12:20,079
Skeletor has imprisoned me
within this energy field

145
00:12:20,123 --> 00:12:23,211
which only he can dissolve.

146
00:12:23,254 --> 00:12:25,906
You are in danger here.
You must leave.

147
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:27,732
We won't leave
without you, Sorceress.

148
00:12:27,775 --> 00:12:30,298
Gwildor, can your key
open a door to the force field?

149
00:12:30,341 --> 00:12:32,211
- Of course.
- [He-Man] Then do it now.

150
00:12:32,254 --> 00:12:34,864
- It'll take time.
- Let's get started then, Gwildor.

151
00:12:34,907 --> 00:12:37,820
- [Man-at-Arms] Gwildor,
over here. - Oh. Uh, uh...

152
00:12:37,864 --> 00:12:41,473
I have to take a reading and
compute the gravitonic tones.

153
00:12:41,516 --> 00:12:43,168
He's taking your power.

154
00:12:43,212 --> 00:12:46,908
I can withstand him
until moonrise.

155
00:12:46,952 --> 00:12:49,603
Until the Great Eye
opens on the universe.

156
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:52,821
- They're coming.
- [Gwildor] Ah!

157
00:12:52,865 --> 00:12:54,995
Gwildor, get back there.
Keep working.

158
00:12:55,039 --> 00:12:56,648
[footsteps approaching]

159
00:12:56,691 --> 00:12:58,300
[Man-at-Arms] Come on. Come on.

160
00:13:24,519 --> 00:13:26,998
Everything comes
to he who waits.

161
00:13:29,693 --> 00:13:36,042
And I have waited so very long
for this moment.

162
00:13:36,085 --> 00:13:37,825
Let her go.

163
00:13:37,869 --> 00:13:39,129
I don't think so.

164
00:13:40,086 --> 00:13:42,433
No.

165
00:13:42,477 --> 00:13:45,869
While she remains imprisoned
within this field,

166
00:13:45,912 --> 00:13:50,999
her powers increase my own, and
when the moon reaches its zenith,

167
00:13:51,043 --> 00:13:53,304
the Great Eye will open

168
00:13:53,347 --> 00:13:56,392
and all the powers of Grayskull

169
00:13:56,434 --> 00:13:58,826
will be bestowed upon me.

170
00:13:58,870 --> 00:14:02,913
Your wondrous Sorceress
will die.

171
00:14:02,957 --> 00:14:04,871
You dare threaten her life?

172
00:14:04,914 --> 00:14:07,045
I dare anything.

173
00:14:07,088 --> 00:14:10,219
I am Skeletor.

174
00:14:10,262 --> 00:14:14,436
Throw down your weapons
and pledge yourselves to me,

175
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:16,306
or you will join her.

176
00:14:16,349 --> 00:14:18,523
It's not her you want, it's me.

177
00:14:18,567 --> 00:14:20,654
It's always been between us.

178
00:14:20,697 --> 00:14:21,872
[Skeletor] Silence.

179
00:14:21,915 --> 00:14:23,567
[key beeping]

180
00:14:23,610 --> 00:14:25,741
It's the locksmith.

181
00:14:25,784 --> 00:14:27,568
The little worm has another key.

182
00:14:27,611 --> 00:14:28,872
What?

183
00:14:28,915 --> 00:14:29,916
No.

184
00:14:31,089 --> 00:14:32,350
Kill him!

185
00:14:34,090 --> 00:14:36,524
- Cover Gwildor! Keep working.
- [weapons firing]

186
00:14:56,918 --> 00:14:58,526
Gwildor.

187
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:00,439
Can that thing
get us out of here?

188
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:02,962
It will. It will. But where?

189
00:15:03,005 --> 00:15:05,005
Anywhere. Just do it fast.

190
00:15:05,049 --> 00:15:06,658
Yes, yes, yes.

191
00:15:06,701 --> 00:15:08,658
[beeps]

192
00:15:11,527 --> 00:15:13,788
It's working.

193
00:15:13,832 --> 00:15:15,832
It's working, it's working.

194
00:15:23,659 --> 00:15:26,441
Man-at-Arms, Teela. I did it!

195
00:15:26,485 --> 00:15:27,659
[laughing]

196
00:15:29,007 --> 00:15:32,007
The door. It's open.
Let's go. He-Man!

197
00:15:32,051 --> 00:15:34,051
No! I won't leave her!

198
00:15:34,094 --> 00:15:37,094
But you must. Eternia needs
you alive, He-Man.

199
00:15:37,138 --> 00:15:39,312
You still have
until moonrise. Go.

200
00:15:44,703 --> 00:15:47,052
He-Man, let's move.
Come on, go.

201
00:15:48,269 --> 00:15:49,443
Come on, Gwildor.

202
00:15:51,313 --> 00:15:52,487
Stop him!

203
00:15:54,227 --> 00:15:56,096
Gwildor, come on!

204
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:58,053
The door! The door!

205
00:16:04,227 --> 00:16:05,314
[Gwildor yells]

206
00:16:05,357 --> 00:16:07,488
- Gwildor!
- [Gwildor] My key.

207
00:16:07,531 --> 00:16:09,618
[Skeletor] The key.
Get the key.

208
00:16:27,229 --> 00:16:30,446
Find them. Trace them!

209
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:33,490
I want them and that key
hunted down and brought to me.

210
00:16:33,533 --> 00:16:36,099
It looked as if he was
punching the keys at random.

211
00:16:36,143 --> 00:16:39,621
- There's no way of telling where they went.
- Monitor the frequencies.

212
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:44,186
Wherever they are, they'll use
it again. When they do, lock it in.

213
00:16:44,230 --> 00:16:48,405
He-Man lives
and possesses that key.

214
00:16:48,448 --> 00:16:52,318
I must possess all
or I possess nothing.

215
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:54,622
Find them.

216
00:16:57,971 --> 00:16:59,753
[whooshing]

217
00:17:14,667 --> 00:17:16,537
[Gwildor hooting]

218
00:17:24,450 --> 00:17:26,668
[Gwildor sputtering]

219
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,451
[both chuckling]

220
00:17:30,711 --> 00:17:33,321
- Are you all right?
- Brrr!

221
00:17:33,364 --> 00:17:35,669
Trust a Thenurian
to find a soft place to land.

222
00:17:36,799 --> 00:17:38,235
[coughing]

223
00:17:39,104 --> 00:17:40,930
Thank you.

224
00:17:40,974 --> 00:17:44,235
I could have suffocated
in that loathsome stuff.

225
00:17:44,278 --> 00:17:47,409
Stop complaining.
It's only mud.

226
00:17:47,452 --> 00:17:50,888
That's easy to say when you
don't have clogged gill slits.

227
00:17:50,931 --> 00:17:52,323
[blowing]

228
00:17:52,365 --> 00:17:55,453
- [Man-at-Arms] Oh, no.
- Oh, I... I'm sorry.

229
00:17:56,497 --> 00:17:58,366
- I'm sorry.
- Gwildor.

230
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,889
Gwildor, we must
get back to Eternia.

231
00:18:00,932 --> 00:18:04,019
So if you're through clearing your gill
slits, maybe you can tell us where we are.

232
00:18:05,106 --> 00:18:06,671
We could be anywhere.

233
00:18:06,714 --> 00:18:08,889
Any planet in the galaxy.

234
00:18:08,932 --> 00:18:11,498
Any planet in
a thousand galaxies.

235
00:18:11,541 --> 00:18:14,846
I had no time to renominalize
my coordinates.

236
00:18:14,890 --> 00:18:17,715
You got us here, you Thenurian
wormbat, now you get us home.

237
00:18:17,759 --> 00:18:21,064
Calm down. Now, we're all
in this together.

238
00:18:21,107 --> 00:18:23,325
How can he get us home
if we don't know where we are?

239
00:18:23,368 --> 00:18:25,064
I'm not a Torktum, you know.

240
00:18:25,107 --> 00:18:29,108
I wouldn't build a device that
didn't store its home coordinates.

241
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:33,847
All we have to do is punch
the energizer switch and...

242
00:18:35,195 --> 00:18:36,326
Uh...

243
00:18:40,717 --> 00:18:43,022
Where is the key?

244
00:18:43,066 --> 00:18:45,587
Perimeter search.
Each of us take a sector.

245
00:18:45,630 --> 00:18:46,717
[rustling in bushes]

246
00:18:46,761 --> 00:18:48,022
- What's that?
- [He-Man] Shh.

247
00:18:57,067 --> 00:18:58,284
[whispers] Scan the area.

248
00:19:02,502 --> 00:19:04,719
Alien life form. Big.

249
00:19:04,763 --> 00:19:06,110
- Let me blast it.
- Wait.

250
00:19:06,154 --> 00:19:07,328
It might be intelligent life.

251
00:19:09,111 --> 00:19:11,285
[branches rustling]

252
00:19:11,329 --> 00:19:12,981
By the Sorceress, it's ugly.

253
00:19:13,981 --> 00:19:14,981
It seems harmless.

254
00:19:17,677 --> 00:19:19,416
[moos]

255
00:19:19,459 --> 00:19:22,025
What a hideous cry.

256
00:19:22,069 --> 00:19:24,459
Maybe I can communicate
with the poor creature.

257
00:19:24,503 --> 00:19:27,025
- Gwildor.
- [Gwildor mooing]

258
00:19:27,069 --> 00:19:28,112
Gwildor.

259
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,895
Gwildor, we have
very little time.

260
00:19:31,938 --> 00:19:35,504
He-Man, I show 0.84 chromons
until moonrise at Grayskull.

261
00:19:35,547 --> 00:19:38,547
- We'd better find the key, and fast.
- What's your plan?

262
00:19:38,591 --> 00:19:41,721
When we find the key, Gwildor
will set coordinates for Grayskull.

263
00:19:41,765 --> 00:19:43,113
We'll use the element
of surprise.

264
00:19:43,157 --> 00:19:45,374
Oh, sure, we'll drop
right into the throne room,

265
00:19:45,418 --> 00:19:48,157
fight off two or three thousand
of Skeletor's crack troops,

266
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:50,245
break into the force field
and free the Sorceress.

267
00:19:50,288 --> 00:19:51,984
- Right.
- [Man-at-Arms] If we're gonna split up,

268
00:19:52,027 --> 00:19:54,635
we'd better synchronize
our personal locators.

269
00:19:54,679 --> 00:19:55,897
You both ready? And...

270
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:56,897
[both devices beep]

271
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:58,898
If you find the key,

272
00:19:58,941 --> 00:20:00,898
- activate the sourcing signal.
- [Man-at-Arms and Teela] The sourcing signal.

273
00:20:00,941 --> 00:20:02,159
- Good journey.
- Good journey.

274
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,375
Good journey.

275
00:20:05,941 --> 00:20:06,898
Moo.

276
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,550
Moo?

277
00:20:11,941 --> 00:20:13,942
Moo!

278
00:20:13,986 --> 00:20:17,594
- [He-Man] Gwildor.
- I'm going. I'm going. Moo.

279
00:20:21,334 --> 00:20:24,029
[country music playing
over jukebox]

280
00:20:24,073 --> 00:20:26,943
- Thanks. Come again.
- [customer] Sure thing, ma'am.

281
00:20:26,987 --> 00:20:29,248
[man] Billy, get off the game
and get Daddy some napkins.

282
00:20:29,290 --> 00:20:31,378
[door closes]

283
00:20:31,421 --> 00:20:34,378
I never thought I'd feel sad about
doing that for the very last time.

284
00:20:34,422 --> 00:20:37,857
[chuckles softly] Don't worry,
Julie. They've got fast food in Jersey.

285
00:20:37,901 --> 00:20:38,901
Thanks a lot.

286
00:20:40,813 --> 00:20:44,639
I got a going-away present
for you, but it isn't wrapped.

287
00:20:44,683 --> 00:20:47,423
- You didn't have to do that.
- It isn't even in a box.

288
00:20:47,466 --> 00:20:49,814
It's a piece of advice, and I
pray to God you listen to it.

289
00:20:51,988 --> 00:20:54,510
If you break up
with Kevin Corrigan,

290
00:20:54,553 --> 00:20:56,727
you will regret it
for the rest of your life.

291
00:20:56,771 --> 00:20:59,511
Monica, this is not
the seventh grade anymore.

292
00:20:59,554 --> 00:21:03,076
Kevin's changed. I've changed.
Everything's different now.

293
00:21:03,119 --> 00:21:05,076
Fine. Except for two things.

294
00:21:05,119 --> 00:21:07,903
A, you still love him,
and B, he still loves you.

295
00:21:07,946 --> 00:21:09,990
Kevin doesn't need me
or my problems right now.

296
00:21:11,946 --> 00:21:13,512
I just feel if I stayed...

297
00:21:13,555 --> 00:21:15,773
Julie, I know it's
hard right now,

298
00:21:15,815 --> 00:21:18,468
but you don't have to move away.

299
00:21:18,512 --> 00:21:22,773
- Yes, I do. - Your folks
would've wanted you to stay.

300
00:21:22,816 --> 00:21:26,556
The best thing for me to do right now
is to get 3000 miles away from Kevin,

301
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:29,730
my house, this town and
everything, and just start out fresh.

302
00:21:30,295 --> 00:21:32,556
[car horn beeps]

303
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,513
- That's Kevin.
- Oh, I'm gonna miss you.

304
00:21:40,992 --> 00:21:43,079
[soulful '80s
rock music playing]

305
00:21:44,601 --> 00:21:47,383
So, uh, what time's your bus
to the airport?

306
00:21:47,427 --> 00:21:49,514
- 8:30.
- Oh, great.

307
00:21:49,557 --> 00:21:51,080
So you can make
my sound check, right?

308
00:21:52,558 --> 00:21:54,167
- Yeah?
- [chuckles softly]

309
00:21:54,210 --> 00:21:57,950
- Yes, I'll make your sound check.
- [chuckles] All right.

310
00:21:57,994 --> 00:22:01,907
- Oh, I brought us dinner.
- Oh, boy, Robby's ribs.

311
00:22:01,950 --> 00:22:04,472
- Yeah, I thought something
different for a change. - Oh, yes.

312
00:22:04,515 --> 00:22:06,342
[both chuckle]

313
00:22:06,385 --> 00:22:08,124
Yeah, well, it's not very
romantic for our last date.

314
00:22:12,777 --> 00:22:15,559
Look, Julie, why don't you
take a later flight, huh? And...

315
00:22:15,603 --> 00:22:17,733
Kevin, don't start that again.

316
00:22:18,690 --> 00:22:19,690
We decided.

317
00:22:22,430 --> 00:22:23,734
[smacks lips] Okay.

318
00:22:25,647 --> 00:22:28,996
[Julie] Kevin, I'd like to go to the
cemetery to say goodbye to my parents.

319
00:22:29,039 --> 00:22:30,734
[Kevin] Yeah, sure.

320
00:22:49,345 --> 00:22:51,519
[Man-at-Arms gasps]

321
00:22:51,562 --> 00:22:53,345
Don't ever sneak up
on me like that.

322
00:22:53,388 --> 00:22:56,041
This is my sector.
You're not supposed to be here.

323
00:22:56,085 --> 00:22:58,389
An old soldier learns
to follow his nose.

324
00:22:58,433 --> 00:23:02,128
- Oh, Father, you're always hungry.
- I'm not always hungry.

325
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:04,259
During the Siege of Krey,
30 days...

326
00:23:04,302 --> 00:23:06,259
[both] Without rations.

327
00:23:06,302 --> 00:23:09,260
Father, the Sorceress.
We must find the key.

328
00:23:09,303 --> 00:23:11,694
We're not gonna save Eternia
if we die of starvation.

329
00:23:12,999 --> 00:23:14,347
Wait. Look.

330
00:23:16,521 --> 00:23:19,130
[Man-at-Arms] I was doing that
before you were born.

331
00:23:19,173 --> 00:23:21,913
[Teela] Not the natives,
Father. There, in the bushes.

332
00:23:23,738 --> 00:23:24,913
[smacking lips]

333
00:23:30,261 --> 00:23:31,087
[both moaning]

334
00:23:33,001 --> 00:23:33,870
[both] Gwildor.

335
00:23:48,132 --> 00:23:49,089
Holding out on us, huh?

336
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:51,437
[laughs]

337
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:55,350
Just in time. I was going to
share. I was going to share.

338
00:23:55,393 --> 00:23:57,350
[Man-at-Arms] Sure you were.

339
00:23:57,393 --> 00:23:58,611
[Gwildor cackling]

340
00:23:59,003 --> 00:23:59,916
Teela.

341
00:24:01,307 --> 00:24:04,090
Mm! Good food.

342
00:24:04,133 --> 00:24:08,133
Yes, I've never tasted
anything like it.

343
00:24:08,177 --> 00:24:10,568
I wonder why they put their
food on these little white sticks.

344
00:24:11,394 --> 00:24:12,220
Those are rib bones.

345
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:18,308
[coughs]

346
00:24:18,352 --> 00:24:20,917
- You mean this used
to be an animal?- Mm-hm.

347
00:24:22,265 --> 00:24:23,656
[Teela] Ugh.

348
00:24:26,005 --> 00:24:28,526
Ugh, what a barbaric world.

349
00:24:28,569 --> 00:24:30,743
Never think while you're hungry.

350
00:24:30,787 --> 00:24:33,222
I think we've wasted
enough time.

351
00:24:33,266 --> 00:24:34,919
We better get back
to our sectors.

352
00:24:38,222 --> 00:24:40,093
Gwildor.

353
00:24:40,136 --> 00:24:42,136
It tasted good.

354
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:45,484
- Gwildor.
- Oh, I'm going. I'm going.

355
00:24:48,615 --> 00:24:52,658
[Julie] I never told anyone this
before, but it's my fault they died.

356
00:24:54,484 --> 00:24:56,007
Julie, come on.

357
00:24:58,572 --> 00:25:01,355
It was a plane crash.
Those things just happen.

358
00:25:04,138 --> 00:25:05,138
You don't understand.

359
00:25:07,485 --> 00:25:11,356
We were all supposed to go
to the beach that day.

360
00:25:11,399 --> 00:25:13,530
But I said I had to study because I
wanted to spend the day with you.

361
00:25:17,399 --> 00:25:19,270
So they took the plane
to Catalina instead.

362
00:25:20,965 --> 00:25:22,139
Hey, come on.

363
00:25:27,009 --> 00:25:29,923
Your mom and dad wouldn't want you to go
around the rest of your life blaming yourself.

364
00:25:31,444 --> 00:25:33,748
- Would they?
- No.

365
00:25:40,271 --> 00:25:41,575
God, I wish...

366
00:25:42,532 --> 00:25:44,401
I wish I could change things.

367
00:25:45,098 --> 00:25:46,098
[sniffling]

368
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,141
But you can't.

369
00:25:49,489 --> 00:25:51,489
That only happens
in fairy tales.

370
00:25:57,142 --> 00:25:59,489
[key beeping]

371
00:25:59,533 --> 00:26:01,142
[Julie] What is that?

372
00:26:01,186 --> 00:26:03,229
[Kevin] Wow! Whoa,
Julie, be careful.

373
00:26:03,273 --> 00:26:04,837
Kev, look at this thing.

374
00:26:06,316 --> 00:26:09,229
Whoa! That is incredible.
What is it?

375
00:26:09,273 --> 00:26:11,100
I don't know. Someone must
have dropped it.

376
00:26:11,143 --> 00:26:13,926
Dropped it, are you kidding?
Look at the size of that hole.

377
00:26:13,969 --> 00:26:15,535
It's like it fell out
of the sky or something.

378
00:26:16,317 --> 00:26:17,969
[both laughing]

379
00:26:18,013 --> 00:26:21,230
No. This is one of those
new Japanese synthesizers.

380
00:26:21,274 --> 00:26:22,709
- Here, let me try it.
- Okay.

381
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:24,883
[key sounds chord]

382
00:26:24,927 --> 00:26:26,144
Whoa! [laughs]

383
00:26:26,188 --> 00:26:28,449
Listen to this.
Oh, this is hot.

384
00:26:29,665 --> 00:26:32,014
[key playing musical notes]

385
00:26:32,057 --> 00:26:34,144
We've got to turn this
in to the caretaker.

386
00:26:34,188 --> 00:26:36,492
Oh, no way, come on, are you
kidding? He'd just keep this for himself.

387
00:26:43,015 --> 00:26:44,971
[Evil-Lyn] The Cosmic Key
has been activated.

388
00:26:45,015 --> 00:26:48,929
- We have a bearing on them.
- How accurate?

389
00:26:48,972 --> 00:26:50,363
Within a parsec eon.

390
00:26:52,493 --> 00:26:54,667
The next time they use the key,

391
00:26:54,711 --> 00:26:57,885
lock in the source
and open a doorway.

392
00:26:57,929 --> 00:26:59,407
Shall I prepare
a full battalion?

393
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,973
No. It may be a trap.

394
00:27:02,017 --> 00:27:04,625
We'll send an advance group.

395
00:27:04,668 --> 00:27:06,408
Assemble the mercenaries.

396
00:27:09,321 --> 00:27:12,060
Have faith, Sorceress.

397
00:27:12,104 --> 00:27:13,713
You won't be lonely long.

398
00:27:14,669 --> 00:27:15,626
[chuckles]

399
00:27:20,018 --> 00:27:21,583
[car honking]

400
00:27:35,584 --> 00:27:38,454
Julie. Here, listen to this.

401
00:27:38,497 --> 00:27:40,062
[key playing musical notes]

402
00:27:44,541 --> 00:27:46,715
- What do you think?
- Sounds great.

403
00:27:48,281 --> 00:27:49,585
Okay.

404
00:27:51,107 --> 00:27:52,716
I want to see what
this thing can really do.

405
00:27:54,324 --> 00:27:56,846
Test. Test, test. Hello, test.

406
00:27:58,498 --> 00:27:59,716
Here, hold that.

407
00:28:01,151 --> 00:28:02,759
What are you going to do?

408
00:28:02,803 --> 00:28:05,717
I'm going to amp this baby up.
See how it sounds.

409
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:07,717
- All right, are you ready?
- Mm-hm.

410
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:08,717
Hold on.

411
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:11,370
All right, here goes.

412
00:28:15,717 --> 00:28:17,761
[key playing musical note]

413
00:28:22,544 --> 00:28:23,674
- Wow!
- [both chuckle]

414
00:28:27,371 --> 00:28:28,761
I can't believe this.

415
00:28:30,545 --> 00:28:32,371
Override complete.

416
00:28:32,414 --> 00:28:35,024
We're locking in
on the key's source of origin.

417
00:28:35,067 --> 00:28:37,285
Very good. Excellent.

418
00:28:37,328 --> 00:28:39,937
[Skeletor] You are
too easily pleased, Evil-Lyn.

419
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:42,589
Have you forgotten
time is of the essence?

420
00:28:43,372 --> 00:28:44,502
Show me.

421
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:51,720
There. That's close enough.

422
00:28:54,634 --> 00:28:56,677
Have you assembled
the mercenaries?

423
00:28:56,721 --> 00:28:58,460
Here, and awaiting your command.

424
00:29:00,026 --> 00:29:03,026
I have selected
your finest warriors.

425
00:29:04,113 --> 00:29:05,026
Blade.

426
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,330
Saurod.

427
00:29:11,113 --> 00:29:12,287
[growls]

428
00:29:13,156 --> 00:29:14,156
The Beastman.

429
00:29:15,114 --> 00:29:16,548
[growls]

430
00:29:17,070 --> 00:29:18,504
And Karg.

431
00:29:22,027 --> 00:29:23,070
[Skeletor] Hmm.

432
00:29:24,157 --> 00:29:26,114
A curious quartet.

433
00:29:27,897 --> 00:29:30,679
He-Man has slipped away from me.

434
00:29:30,723 --> 00:29:32,549
I want him back.

435
00:29:32,592 --> 00:29:35,506
This must happen
before moonrise.

436
00:29:35,550 --> 00:29:38,637
Now, you are to go through to
this world to where they are hiding,

437
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,289
find the key,

438
00:29:40,332 --> 00:29:43,376
do as you wish with the others,
but bring He-Man back alive.

439
00:29:45,072 --> 00:29:46,072
You do understand?

440
00:29:46,116 --> 00:29:47,681
[all] Yes, lord.

441
00:29:48,898 --> 00:29:49,725
Good.

442
00:29:52,072 --> 00:29:54,290
Open the door.
Do not fail me.

443
00:29:57,030 --> 00:29:59,552
I... I can't
believe this thing.

444
00:29:59,595 --> 00:30:01,595
I mean, did you see
those lights, huh?

445
00:30:01,639 --> 00:30:03,943
Look, we've gotta take this
down to Charlie.

446
00:30:03,986 --> 00:30:05,247
He's... He's gotta
know what this is.

447
00:30:05,291 --> 00:30:07,334
No, you go ahead.

448
00:30:07,378 --> 00:30:11,335
This sounds really strange, but I kinda
want to spend some time here alone.

449
00:30:11,379 --> 00:30:14,987
Say goodbye to the place. I'm
not gonna be here for graduation.

450
00:30:15,031 --> 00:30:18,118
Look, look, Julie, um, I'll just
go by Charlie's later, okay?

451
00:30:18,161 --> 00:30:19,945
No, no, go ahead, I promise.

452
00:30:19,988 --> 00:30:22,379
- Are you sure?
- Mm-hm.

453
00:30:22,422 --> 00:30:25,814
Okay, all right. I'll be gone
15 minutes, tops. All right?

454
00:30:25,857 --> 00:30:28,945
- Don't let anybody in here
except Carl. - All right.

455
00:30:28,988 --> 00:30:31,293
Hear me? Bye.

456
00:30:31,336 --> 00:30:32,902
- I'll guard this stuff for you.
- All right. Bye.

457
00:30:55,599 --> 00:30:56,773
[whooshing]

458
00:31:08,339 --> 00:31:09,339
Carl?

459
00:31:19,166 --> 00:31:20,949
[Karg jabbering]

460
00:31:22,558 --> 00:31:24,775
Carl, is that you?

461
00:31:24,819 --> 00:31:26,819
- Blade.
- Deserted. No sign of the key.

462
00:31:26,862 --> 00:31:29,732
Scan the perimeter.
No one in, no one out.

463
00:31:29,775 --> 00:31:31,167
Kevin, if this is
some kind of joke,

464
00:31:31,211 --> 00:31:32,341
it's... It's really not funny.

465
00:31:34,906 --> 00:31:36,733
Listen, you kids can't
just come in...

466
00:31:38,994 --> 00:31:40,255
Don't kill him yet.

467
00:31:40,776 --> 00:31:41,776
[grunts]

468
00:31:45,386 --> 00:31:46,342
[Beastman growling]

469
00:31:46,386 --> 00:31:47,560
[screams]

470
00:31:49,516 --> 00:31:50,560
[Julie] Leave him alone!

471
00:31:54,169 --> 00:31:54,952
[screams]

472
00:31:56,647 --> 00:31:58,952
Somebody help me.
Somebody help me!

473
00:32:00,864 --> 00:32:04,474
No, no. Take her alive.
She may know where the key is.

474
00:32:07,170 --> 00:32:08,561
Over there.

475
00:32:08,604 --> 00:32:10,170
That way. Go around.

476
00:32:15,388 --> 00:32:16,910
[Julie screaming]

477
00:32:20,171 --> 00:32:21,779
[growling]

478
00:32:23,084 --> 00:32:23,910
[screams]

479
00:32:26,650 --> 00:32:28,302
- I've got you, pretty!
- No!

480
00:32:29,563 --> 00:32:30,955
No!

481
00:32:30,998 --> 00:32:32,519
Let go, stay away from me!

482
00:32:32,563 --> 00:32:33,563
Let go!

483
00:32:34,519 --> 00:32:35,606
Get her.

484
00:32:39,694 --> 00:32:41,129
She's mine.

485
00:32:41,172 --> 00:32:42,651
[screams] Ah!

486
00:32:47,043 --> 00:32:48,130
[growling]

487
00:32:49,260 --> 00:32:50,565
[roars]

488
00:32:52,130 --> 00:32:54,130
Stop her!

489
00:32:54,173 --> 00:32:54,956
[Julie] Somebody help!

490
00:32:56,086 --> 00:32:57,521
- [yells]
- [growls]

491
00:32:59,652 --> 00:33:03,435
Move, you animals.
Go, go, go!

492
00:33:04,609 --> 00:33:06,827
Find her. Find her!

493
00:33:14,088 --> 00:33:15,696
[beeping]

494
00:33:16,740 --> 00:33:19,262
[Julie] Help me! Help me!

495
00:33:20,567 --> 00:33:21,871
[rapid beeping]

496
00:33:24,133 --> 00:33:25,567
Somebody help me!

497
00:33:27,523 --> 00:33:29,263
Oh, God, help.

498
00:33:34,829 --> 00:33:36,742
[Blade] She's in there.
This way.

499
00:33:38,698 --> 00:33:40,785
[yelling]

500
00:33:48,612 --> 00:33:51,264
She's in here somewhere.
Find her!

501
00:33:58,744 --> 00:33:59,917
[Julie screams]

502
00:33:59,961 --> 00:34:02,135
- Get away from me.
- [He-Man] It's all right.

503
00:34:02,178 --> 00:34:05,570
It's all right. Don't be
afraid, I won't hurt you.

504
00:34:05,613 --> 00:34:06,744
Now, what are you running from?

505
00:34:08,484 --> 00:34:10,658
I'm running
from these... These...

506
00:34:10,700 --> 00:34:12,962
- Monsters.
- Easy, easy.

507
00:34:13,005 --> 00:34:14,875
- These creatures...
- I'll take care of it.

508
00:34:17,614 --> 00:34:18,745
Look in there.

509
00:34:21,485 --> 00:34:22,963
You, look up that way.

510
00:34:23,963 --> 00:34:24,875
Search over there.

511
00:34:27,137 --> 00:34:28,615
- You. Over there.
- No.

512
00:34:29,702 --> 00:34:31,398
Search in there. Hurry!

513
00:34:33,225 --> 00:34:34,789
[growling]

514
00:34:38,094 --> 00:34:39,660
Here, take this.

515
00:34:40,703 --> 00:34:41,573
Protect yourself.

516
00:34:44,312 --> 00:34:46,008
[boxes falling]

517
00:34:46,052 --> 00:34:47,139
She's over here.

518
00:34:48,052 --> 00:34:48,965
This way.

519
00:34:50,574 --> 00:34:52,052
[growling]

520
00:35:09,749 --> 00:35:10,705
[steel pings]

521
00:35:29,011 --> 00:35:29,793
No!

522
00:35:34,838 --> 00:35:35,969
[He-Man grunting]

523
00:35:49,752 --> 00:35:51,708
I've waited
a long time for this.

524
00:35:52,795 --> 00:35:53,578
[grunts]

525
00:35:58,448 --> 00:36:00,100
[both grunting]

526
00:36:07,927 --> 00:36:08,927
My sword.

527
00:36:12,841 --> 00:36:14,449
[grunts]

528
00:36:14,493 --> 00:36:15,580
Pretty.

529
00:36:25,015 --> 00:36:25,755
No!

530
00:36:31,798 --> 00:36:33,103
- [growling]
- [weapons firing]

531
00:36:36,408 --> 00:36:38,930
[Karg] Retreat. Retreat!

532
00:36:49,148 --> 00:36:52,104
Follow them. They must have
a doorway to Eternia.

533
00:36:52,148 --> 00:36:53,148
Are you all right?

534
00:36:55,192 --> 00:36:57,365
They're gone now.
You're safe.

535
00:36:57,409 --> 00:36:59,062
You're safe.
Do you understand?

536
00:37:00,540 --> 00:37:02,018
[sniffling]

537
00:37:02,062 --> 00:37:04,192
Good. I know you've been
through a great deal,

538
00:37:05,105 --> 00:37:06,627
but I need your help.

539
00:37:06,671 --> 00:37:08,671
[rock 'n' roll music playing]

540
00:37:16,585 --> 00:37:19,454
Hey, hey, hey! Charlie.

541
00:37:19,498 --> 00:37:22,933
- Charlie!
- Hey, Kev, how are you?

542
00:37:22,977 --> 00:37:25,412
Hey, turn that down,
turn that down.

543
00:37:25,455 --> 00:37:27,412
Look, wait until you see this.

544
00:37:27,455 --> 00:37:30,847
Oh, hey, I heard you were
good last night at Club Zero.

545
00:37:30,890 --> 00:37:33,325
Oh, thanks. Thanks. No,
we're going to be better tonight.

546
00:37:33,368 --> 00:37:36,325
- I want you to take a look at
this baby, huh? - All right.

547
00:37:36,368 --> 00:37:37,282
All right, here.

548
00:37:39,326 --> 00:37:40,760
What do you think?

549
00:37:40,803 --> 00:37:41,934
I've seen these before.

550
00:37:42,890 --> 00:37:44,674
- You have?
- Yeah.

551
00:37:44,717 --> 00:37:47,674
- It's Japanese.
- Oh, no, no, no.

552
00:37:47,717 --> 00:37:50,196
I don't think so.
Here, look.

553
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:52,370
Press a few of these buttons.
Go ahead.

554
00:37:53,804 --> 00:37:56,022
[key plays chord]

555
00:37:56,066 --> 00:37:57,979
Huh? Now press that
red button in the front.

556
00:37:58,631 --> 00:37:59,631
Go ahead.

557
00:38:00,805 --> 00:38:03,154
[key plays musical notes]

558
00:38:08,197 --> 00:38:10,980
- Far out. Fantastic.
- [laughs]

559
00:38:12,806 --> 00:38:15,502
[Kevin clears throat]

560
00:38:15,545 --> 00:38:19,198
You know, I guess if you've seen
one, you've seen them all, right?

561
00:38:19,242 --> 00:38:21,198
Thanks a lot, Charlie. You
know, I'll talk to you later.

562
00:38:21,242 --> 00:38:22,416
Hey, come back here.
Come back here.

563
00:38:22,459 --> 00:38:24,111
- What?
- Where'd you get that?

564
00:38:24,155 --> 00:38:27,025
- You wanna sell it?
- No, no. Look, I don't wanna sell it.

565
00:38:27,069 --> 00:38:30,330
Charlie, I found this at Laurelwood.
Man, you would not believe it.

566
00:38:30,373 --> 00:38:33,373
It was like... It was lying
in this huge crater, you know.

567
00:38:33,417 --> 00:38:35,591
I don't know, I was just hoping
you'd know something about it.

568
00:38:35,634 --> 00:38:37,417
I never saw anything like it.

569
00:38:37,460 --> 00:38:38,939
- [Kevin] Look, Charlie, we gotta
figure out... - [sirens blaring]

570
00:38:38,983 --> 00:38:40,157
- What's that?
- ...how, um...

571
00:38:40,199 --> 00:38:41,330
[key plays note]

572
00:38:41,373 --> 00:38:42,765
D sharp.

573
00:38:42,808 --> 00:38:45,418
Oh, Mr. Perfect-Pitch.
[chuckles]

574
00:38:45,461 --> 00:38:47,418
[police sirens blaring]

575
00:38:47,461 --> 00:38:50,722
Whoa! All hell's breaking loose
out there. Let's see what's up.

576
00:38:54,114 --> 00:38:56,114
[woman over police scanner]
<i>All units, Code 6.</i>

577
00:38:56,158 --> 00:38:57,809
<i>Proceed to Central High School.</i>

578
00:38:57,853 --> 00:39:00,071
<i>Fire and vandalism.
Possible arson.</i>

579
00:39:00,114 --> 00:39:02,375
<i>Repeat. All units, Code 6.</i>

580
00:39:02,419 --> 00:39:04,767
Oh, my God.

581
00:39:04,810 --> 00:39:05,723
[woman over police scanner] <i>Proceed
to Central High. Fire and vandalism.</i>

582
00:39:05,767 --> 00:39:07,202
Julie's in there.

583
00:39:07,245 --> 00:39:08,985
[woman over police scanner]
<i>Proceed with caution.</i>

584
00:39:09,028 --> 00:39:12,376
Our only hope of defeating
Skeletor is to find the Cosmic Key.

585
00:39:12,420 --> 00:39:15,072
Now, those creatures were
after you for a reason, Julie.

586
00:39:15,115 --> 00:39:16,202
Have you seen it?

587
00:39:17,463 --> 00:39:19,333
It's this large.
It has lights on it.

588
00:39:19,376 --> 00:39:21,594
Wait a minute, I have seen that.

589
00:39:21,637 --> 00:39:23,681
My boyfriend and I found this
thing that had these patterns of light

590
00:39:23,724 --> 00:39:25,073
and this music coming out of it.

591
00:39:25,116 --> 00:39:27,551
That's it.
Where is it?

592
00:39:27,595 --> 00:39:30,203
- Well, Kevin has it.
- He's in terrible danger. Let's go.

593
00:39:31,551 --> 00:39:33,551
- [siren blaring]
- [helicopter hovering]

594
00:39:33,595 --> 00:39:35,725
- [man 1] Let's call it back.
- [man 2] Everything's all clear in the room.

595
00:39:41,422 --> 00:39:42,770
[indistinct chatter]

596
00:39:58,466 --> 00:40:00,640
Carl. Carl, what happened?

597
00:40:00,684 --> 00:40:03,163
You don't never wanna know.

598
00:40:03,206 --> 00:40:06,076
Wait, listen to me.
Carl. Carl, where is Julie?

599
00:40:06,119 --> 00:40:07,598
What happened to Julie?

600
00:40:14,033 --> 00:40:15,685
- There you go.
- [Kevin] Excuse me.

601
00:40:15,728 --> 00:40:18,120
- Where you going?
- Look, my girlfriend's in there, all right?

602
00:40:18,164 --> 00:40:21,773
Kid, we swept the place. The only
person we found was the janitor.

603
00:40:21,816 --> 00:40:24,381
No, you don't understand. I just left
her here ten minutes ago, all right?

604
00:40:24,425 --> 00:40:27,208
I'm telling you, we went
through there with a police dog.

605
00:40:27,252 --> 00:40:29,121
The only stuff we found
in there was right there.

606
00:40:30,816 --> 00:40:33,556
Dear God, that's Julie's.
Where'd you find this?

607
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:35,078
Where do you think we found it?

608
00:40:35,121 --> 00:40:36,948
Listen, we got vandalism, arson,

609
00:40:36,992 --> 00:40:39,252
we got a lot of bad stuff
going on around here, kid.

610
00:40:39,295 --> 00:40:42,904
- What do you know about it?
- Look, I don't know anything about it, all right?

611
00:40:42,948 --> 00:40:44,992
I mean, you're the cop. Why
aren't you looking for her, huh?

612
00:40:45,035 --> 00:40:46,427
What does she look like?

613
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:49,514
Look, she's about 5'5".

614
00:40:49,557 --> 00:40:51,427
She's got short, dark hair.

615
00:40:51,470 --> 00:40:52,383
She was wearing a pink sweater.

616
00:40:52,427 --> 00:40:54,557
Okay.

617
00:40:54,601 --> 00:40:57,167
Is that all you're gonna do,
you're gonna... You're gonna write?

618
00:40:57,210 --> 00:40:59,167
I mean, why aren't you out
doing something, huh?

619
00:40:59,210 --> 00:41:01,950
All right, I'll do something. I'll
take you for a little ride. Let's go.

620
00:41:01,993 --> 00:41:03,123
Oh, great.

621
00:41:03,167 --> 00:41:04,906
What are you doing, huh?
You arresting me?

622
00:41:04,950 --> 00:41:07,211
We're gonna go look for your
girlfriend. Just like you said.

623
00:41:07,255 --> 00:41:09,950
We'll try her house first.
I bet you know where that is.

624
00:41:09,994 --> 00:41:11,516
Harry, do me a favor.

625
00:41:11,559 --> 00:41:14,907
Take that down to Properties,
give me a full report, okay?

626
00:41:14,950 --> 00:41:18,690
And keep the coffee hot. Looks
like it's gonna be a long night.

627
00:41:18,733 --> 00:41:20,820
[fireman] Come on, guys,
let's go. Let's put it out.

628
00:41:25,299 --> 00:41:26,517
- [Man-at-Arms] He-Man,
they got away. - [Julie gasps]

629
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:27,821
Easy, Julie.

630
00:41:28,386 --> 00:41:30,778
What happened?

631
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:33,430
It's all right. These are friends of
mine, Teela and her father, Duncan.

632
00:41:33,473 --> 00:41:35,908
- Man-at-Arms for Eternian
High Command. - This is Julie.

633
00:41:35,952 --> 00:41:38,126
- Hi. - She knows who has
the key. She wants to help us.

634
00:41:38,170 --> 00:41:39,735
- Good.
- Did you have any luck?

635
00:41:39,779 --> 00:41:41,822
Not as much as you, apparently.

636
00:41:41,866 --> 00:41:44,300
We tracked them spinward,
40 metrons.

637
00:41:44,344 --> 00:41:47,345
- And then they disappeared.
- They're only a scouting party.

638
00:41:47,388 --> 00:41:49,605
Now let's find that key
before they return in full force.

639
00:41:49,648 --> 00:41:51,345
- Julie, which way?
- This way.

640
00:41:51,388 --> 00:41:52,214
[metal screeches]

641
00:41:54,214 --> 00:41:56,475
[tires screeching]

642
00:41:56,519 --> 00:41:58,085
[Man-at-Arms]
Take arms. Full power.

643
00:41:59,432 --> 00:42:00,519
Ready.

644
00:42:03,085 --> 00:42:06,520
Native transportation.
A primitive land boat.

645
00:42:06,563 --> 00:42:08,085
- Enter, enter.
- [Man-at-Arms chuckles]

646
00:42:08,128 --> 00:42:09,607
Gwildor.

647
00:42:09,650 --> 00:42:10,999
Well done, Gwildor.

648
00:42:13,303 --> 00:42:16,521
It was an inefficient
combustible system, but I fixed it.

649
00:42:16,564 --> 00:42:19,608
It runs on iucrenos now.
No hydrocarbons needed.

650
00:42:22,216 --> 00:42:24,216
[device beeping]

651
00:42:32,869 --> 00:42:34,826
Why is there still resistance?

652
00:42:38,262 --> 00:42:42,349
The people must know
that I am Grayskull.

653
00:42:42,392 --> 00:42:45,305
I depend upon you
for these things.

654
00:42:46,262 --> 00:42:47,523
You know that.

655
00:42:49,262 --> 00:42:50,089
[Evil-Lyn] The people

656
00:42:51,784 --> 00:42:54,306
wait for He-Man.

657
00:42:54,350 --> 00:42:56,784
They believe that he will
return to lead them.

658
00:42:58,698 --> 00:43:00,567
For you to rule completely,

659
00:43:01,437 --> 00:43:04,828
he must be destroyed.

660
00:43:04,872 --> 00:43:10,046
He-Man. If I kill him,
I make him a martyr, a saint.

661
00:43:10,090 --> 00:43:13,351
No, I want him broken.

662
00:43:13,394 --> 00:43:15,004
[door opens and closes]

663
00:43:33,396 --> 00:43:34,222
Where is the key?

664
00:43:35,222 --> 00:43:37,048
We, uh, uh,

665
00:43:37,092 --> 00:43:40,092
traced the key's signal, uh,

666
00:43:40,135 --> 00:43:43,309
[stutters] but were unable
to take possession of it.

667
00:43:43,353 --> 00:43:45,310
Is that all?

668
00:43:45,354 --> 00:43:49,962
We... We fought with the
Eternians, but were outnumbered.

669
00:43:50,006 --> 00:43:52,528
We thought it wise
to return alive,

670
00:43:52,571 --> 00:43:54,745
and gather a larger force.

671
00:43:54,789 --> 00:43:56,571
So, He-Man's free?

672
00:43:56,615 --> 00:43:57,615
- [gasps]
- [growls]

673
00:43:59,615 --> 00:44:00,832
[stammers]

674
00:44:05,007 --> 00:44:09,355
You are all aware
of the penalty for failure?

675
00:44:09,398 --> 00:44:13,138
Give me one more chance, Lord
Skeletor, and we will succeed.

676
00:44:13,182 --> 00:44:16,530
I am not in
the giving vein this day.

677
00:44:18,269 --> 00:44:20,008
[screeching]

678
00:44:25,052 --> 00:44:25,921
Ha!

679
00:44:29,052 --> 00:44:30,226
[growling]

680
00:44:31,444 --> 00:44:32,574
Get away!

681
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:38,444
He begs your forgiveness,
as do we all.

682
00:44:38,487 --> 00:44:42,401
We... We live
only to serve you.

683
00:44:42,445 --> 00:44:44,749
It would be a pity
to waste their talents.

684
00:44:44,793 --> 00:44:49,141
Save your pity for yourself,
if you fail.

685
00:44:49,185 --> 00:44:52,836
Take them and whatever troops
and resources you need.

686
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:54,706
I was not suggesting that I go.

687
00:44:54,749 --> 00:44:57,141
Then you should not have spoken.

688
00:44:57,185 --> 00:44:58,794
Leave immediately.

689
00:44:58,837 --> 00:45:02,099
When you find the key,
send the sourcing signal.

690
00:45:02,142 --> 00:45:05,968
An attack force will join you
or I will follow.

691
00:45:11,186 --> 00:45:12,012
Go!

692
00:45:30,057 --> 00:45:32,275
Maybe your girlfriend's here.
The lights are on.

693
00:45:32,318 --> 00:45:34,405
No, no. They leave that on
to scare off burglars.

694
00:45:34,449 --> 00:45:36,101
Oh, yeah? Let's go see.

695
00:45:42,449 --> 00:45:44,363
Hey, not so fast, kid.

696
00:45:46,450 --> 00:45:48,624
[dialing]

697
00:45:50,189 --> 00:45:51,841
[phone rings]

698
00:45:51,885 --> 00:45:54,319
- Hello?
- Kevin, thank God it's you.

699
00:45:54,363 --> 00:45:57,754
[sighs] Um, Julie's not here
right now.

700
00:45:57,798 --> 00:46:00,885
Kevin, this is Julie.
What's going on?

701
00:46:00,928 --> 00:46:05,233
Well, it's good to hear your voice, too, but,
um, I've been really worried about Julie.

702
00:46:05,277 --> 00:46:07,538
Kevin, is someone there?
Are you okay?

703
00:46:07,581 --> 00:46:10,060
Yeah. That's what
I thought too.

704
00:46:10,104 --> 00:46:12,191
Look, Kevin,
this is really important.

705
00:46:12,234 --> 00:46:15,017
I know you can't talk, just say yes or
no. Do you still have that thing we found?

706
00:46:17,321 --> 00:46:18,756
Mm-hm.

707
00:46:18,800 --> 00:46:20,626
Oh, thank God.

708
00:46:20,669 --> 00:46:22,756
All right, listen.
Don't do anything.

709
00:46:22,800 --> 00:46:24,887
Oh, God, I have so much
to explain to you. I...

710
00:46:24,930 --> 00:46:27,192
All right, just stay there,
we'll be right there, okay?

711
00:46:27,235 --> 00:46:28,235
Stay put, all right?

712
00:46:29,192 --> 00:46:31,801
I love you. Bye.

713
00:46:31,844 --> 00:46:35,193
- Okay, look, if you talk to Julie,
could you tell her... - Wait a minute.

714
00:46:35,236 --> 00:46:38,888
Wait a minute. This is the
police, who is this? Who is this?

715
00:46:38,931 --> 00:46:42,193
- Who were you talking to?
- Um, it was just a friend of Julie's.

716
00:46:42,236 --> 00:46:43,410
- Say, you hungry?
- No.

717
00:46:45,193 --> 00:46:46,628
You were talking about
this thing, weren't you?

718
00:46:51,368 --> 00:46:55,063
- What... What is this thing?
- It's a synthesizer.

719
00:46:55,107 --> 00:46:57,498
- Yeah?
- [key beeping]

720
00:46:57,542 --> 00:47:00,890
- How does this thing work?
- Just press these buttons right here.

721
00:47:00,933 --> 00:47:03,369
- Like this?
- Whoa, whoa, careful, careful.

722
00:47:03,412 --> 00:47:04,499
[playing musical notes]

723
00:47:04,542 --> 00:47:05,716
[laughing]

724
00:47:09,891 --> 00:47:11,369
Do you want
to know something, kid?

725
00:47:13,282 --> 00:47:14,847
I don't think this
is any synthesizer.

726
00:47:15,412 --> 00:47:17,022
[dramatic music]

727
00:47:33,110 --> 00:47:34,979
This is where they ambushed us.

728
00:47:35,023 --> 00:47:36,501
We didn't have a chance.

729
00:47:36,545 --> 00:47:37,936
We'll see. Scanner.

730
00:47:40,414 --> 00:47:42,198
[scanner buzzing]

731
00:47:46,849 --> 00:47:48,328
I see only He-Man.

732
00:47:50,459 --> 00:47:52,372
Where are the forces
that you spoke of?

733
00:47:52,415 --> 00:47:53,850
[stammering]

734
00:47:53,894 --> 00:47:54,763
Ah!

735
00:47:56,416 --> 00:47:59,460
And a native girl.

736
00:47:59,503 --> 00:48:01,808
It must have been she who
tipped the scales against you.

737
00:48:04,590 --> 00:48:05,764
Outnumbered?

738
00:48:07,416 --> 00:48:09,374
Outclassed is more like it.

739
00:48:09,417 --> 00:48:11,113
[centurion] The key
has been activated.

740
00:48:11,156 --> 00:48:12,374
Lock on to the signal.

741
00:48:13,895 --> 00:48:16,330
It's close.
About ten metrons.

742
00:48:16,374 --> 00:48:17,852
[Kevin] You wanna see
what that thing does,

743
00:48:17,896 --> 00:48:19,417
press the red button
down at the bottom.

744
00:48:19,461 --> 00:48:20,809
What? This one?

745
00:48:20,852 --> 00:48:21,635
Whoa!

746
00:48:22,635 --> 00:48:24,244
[key plays chords]

747
00:48:24,288 --> 00:48:25,809
Holy smokes.

748
00:48:27,331 --> 00:48:28,462
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

749
00:48:28,505 --> 00:48:29,810
What are you, a magician?

750
00:48:31,592 --> 00:48:32,853
How...
How do you stop this?

751
00:48:36,028 --> 00:48:37,158
[gasps]

752
00:48:43,115 --> 00:48:45,593
What's a kid like you doing
with something like that, huh?

753
00:48:45,637 --> 00:48:48,159
- Oh. Come on. It's my instrument.
- [chuckles] Yeah.

754
00:48:48,203 --> 00:48:52,072
All right, look, let me heat
this up, then I'll show you, okay?

755
00:48:52,116 --> 00:48:54,768
[centurion] We're getting
interference. They're jamming the signal.

756
00:48:54,812 --> 00:48:58,117
Locate the source of the
jamming and destroy it.

757
00:48:58,159 --> 00:49:00,594
[centurion] It's difficult,
like nothing I've seen before.

758
00:49:00,638 --> 00:49:03,030
Destroy it now.

759
00:49:04,812 --> 00:49:05,725
[glass shatters]

760
00:49:06,769 --> 00:49:08,856
Whoa! Watch... Watch out!

761
00:49:12,508 --> 00:49:14,900
[centurion] The source of
interference is destroyed.

762
00:49:14,943 --> 00:49:17,031
We have a clear signal
from the key.

763
00:49:17,074 --> 00:49:18,813
Lock it in. We'll track it
from the air.

764
00:49:20,640 --> 00:49:23,683
[coughs] Turkey, sit down.

765
00:49:23,727 --> 00:49:26,249
- All right, no more crapping around.
What is this? - I don't know.

766
00:49:26,292 --> 00:49:28,206
Listen, I got vandalism,
I got arson,

767
00:49:28,249 --> 00:49:30,554
I got stuff blowing up
in my face around here.

768
00:49:30,597 --> 00:49:33,597
- Now, you better know something.
- Look, I found it, okay?

769
00:49:33,641 --> 00:49:35,641
You found it? You mean, you
don't know who the owner is?

770
00:49:35,684 --> 00:49:37,989
No.

771
00:49:38,033 --> 00:49:40,467
Listen, I was gonna go put a note
down at Charlie's music store, all right?

772
00:49:40,510 --> 00:49:43,598
You know what I'm gonna do? I'm
gonna take this down to the station,

773
00:49:43,641 --> 00:49:45,468
I'm gonna put it on the
computer, I'm gonna check it out,

774
00:49:45,511 --> 00:49:47,250
see if it's reported stolen.

775
00:49:47,294 --> 00:49:48,816
Now, for the last time, kid,
where'd you find this?

776
00:49:52,208 --> 00:49:56,469
Laurelwood Cemetery.
It was in a flowerbed.

777
00:49:56,512 --> 00:49:59,903
Look, if you don't believe me,
go ask Charlie, all right?

778
00:49:59,946 --> 00:50:03,078
- Go ahead, ask him.
- Boy...

779
00:50:03,121 --> 00:50:06,382
- I just may do that.
- Hey, whoa, you can't just take that.

780
00:50:06,425 --> 00:50:08,556
Oh, yeah? You just watch me.

781
00:50:08,599 --> 00:50:12,209
And don't worry about your girlfriend. We
got an APB out on her. She won't get far.

782
00:50:12,252 --> 00:50:14,426
As far as this thing is
concerned, don't worry about it.

783
00:50:14,470 --> 00:50:16,557
If your story checks out,
you'll get it back.

784
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:19,600
If.

785
00:50:39,906 --> 00:50:41,341
[Beastman growling]

786
00:50:45,428 --> 00:50:48,429
Get out of here! Get out
of here. Get out of here.

787
00:50:51,386 --> 00:50:53,038
[grunting]

788
00:51:01,169 --> 00:51:02,777
What do you want from me?

789
00:51:04,387 --> 00:51:07,169
No! Leave him.

790
00:51:12,822 --> 00:51:16,083
You have the Cosmic Key.
Tell us where it is.

791
00:51:16,127 --> 00:51:18,083
I don't know what you guys
are talking about.

792
00:51:18,127 --> 00:51:20,736
- Let me persuade him.
- No.

793
00:51:20,779 --> 00:51:21,953
The collar.

794
00:51:24,431 --> 00:51:25,779
[grunts]

795
00:51:27,215 --> 00:51:30,779
Please. Look, I don't know
what you want. [grunts]

796
00:51:34,563 --> 00:51:35,650
Now,

797
00:51:37,650 --> 00:51:39,259
you will answer my questions.

798
00:51:41,433 --> 00:51:42,477
Yes.

799
00:51:43,651 --> 00:51:44,694
Yes.

800
00:52:04,913 --> 00:52:06,174
Have you seen

801
00:52:07,305 --> 00:52:08,869
this object?

802
00:52:15,218 --> 00:52:16,218
Yes.

803
00:52:17,827 --> 00:52:18,870
[Evil-Lyn] Where is it?

804
00:52:20,566 --> 00:52:22,262
It was taken from me.

805
00:52:22,306 --> 00:52:23,610
Who took it?

806
00:52:25,915 --> 00:52:27,045
[Kevin] A policeman.

807
00:52:28,436 --> 00:52:29,567
Where is he now?

808
00:52:30,610 --> 00:52:31,741
I don't know. He...

809
00:52:33,394 --> 00:52:35,046
He just left.

810
00:52:35,089 --> 00:52:37,046
We should be able to track
the key from the air.

811
00:52:37,089 --> 00:52:38,263
Yes.

812
00:52:41,133 --> 00:52:42,655
Prepare the transport
immediately.

813
00:52:47,003 --> 00:52:51,221
Wait. Evil-Lyn, I found this.

814
00:52:51,264 --> 00:52:54,786
This is the native girl
who is helping He-Man.

815
00:52:54,830 --> 00:52:57,135
This may prove useful.

816
00:52:57,178 --> 00:52:58,743
[Blade] Into the transport.
Move!

817
00:53:02,786 --> 00:53:04,265
[Blade] Move it out!

818
00:53:04,309 --> 00:53:05,048
Move!

819
00:53:10,179 --> 00:53:11,874
[dramatic music]

820
00:53:54,356 --> 00:53:56,052
- Fan out.
- Moving.

821
00:53:56,095 --> 00:53:57,313
[Man-at-Arms] Looks like
Skeletor got here before us.

822
00:53:57,356 --> 00:53:58,487
It's all clear over here.

823
00:53:58,530 --> 00:53:59,574
- Stay ready.
- Kevin!

824
00:54:00,356 --> 00:54:01,617
[softly] Kevin.

825
00:54:03,487 --> 00:54:05,661
Oh, my God, Kevin, you
all right? He's bleeding.

826
00:54:06,444 --> 00:54:08,270
What happened?

827
00:54:08,314 --> 00:54:11,662
They asked me for the key,
but I didn't have it.

828
00:54:11,705 --> 00:54:14,792
- The Cosmic Key.
- Kevin, did they take it?

829
00:54:15,923 --> 00:54:16,792
No.

830
00:54:18,141 --> 00:54:19,618
A policeman took it.

831
00:54:19,662 --> 00:54:21,576
Where is he now?

832
00:54:21,619 --> 00:54:23,010
What is this thing?

833
00:54:23,054 --> 00:54:25,576
- What's the matter with him?
- Skeletor's work.

834
00:54:25,619 --> 00:54:27,706
The Collar of Aldruber.
They've been questioning him.

835
00:54:27,750 --> 00:54:30,445
- I'll have it off in a moment.
- He'll be all right.

836
00:54:30,489 --> 00:54:31,793
Who put this on you?

837
00:54:32,576 --> 00:54:34,924
A woman.

838
00:54:34,967 --> 00:54:38,446
- Strange eyes.
- Evil-Lyn. She's here.

839
00:54:38,490 --> 00:54:40,403
From the looks of this place,
she definitely wasn't alone.

840
00:54:40,446 --> 00:54:42,012
- Right.
- Oh!

841
00:54:42,056 --> 00:54:43,838
- You all right?
- [Kevin grunts]

842
00:54:46,099 --> 00:54:49,882
Julie. Julie,
get out of here. Now!

843
00:54:51,143 --> 00:54:53,186
Ow! Damn.

844
00:54:53,230 --> 00:54:56,839
- Kevin, these are my friends.
- Your friends? Julie.

845
00:54:56,882 --> 00:55:00,839
Look, will somebody tell me
what the hell is going on here, huh?

846
00:55:00,882 --> 00:55:02,361
I mean, all of a sudden, these creatures
come in and start to beat the crap...

847
00:55:02,405 --> 00:55:04,057
Kevin, listen to me.

848
00:55:04,100 --> 00:55:06,448
These people are
fighting the others.

849
00:55:06,492 --> 00:55:09,058
- They saved my life, now trust me.
- Trust you?

850
00:55:09,101 --> 00:55:12,014
Julie, I swear to God,
these, these

851
00:55:12,058 --> 00:55:14,536
things come in here...
I mean, look at this place.

852
00:55:14,580 --> 00:55:16,406
[Gwildor clears throat]

853
00:55:16,449 --> 00:55:20,015
Look. Look. Native clothing.
Lots of it, all over the place.

854
00:55:20,059 --> 00:55:22,015
[all laughing]

855
00:55:22,059 --> 00:55:25,102
If we dress like this,
no one will recognize us.

856
00:55:25,146 --> 00:55:27,841
- What the hell is that?
- See? [laughs]

857
00:55:27,884 --> 00:55:31,363
That's Gwildor. Look, Kevin,
I'll explain to you as we go.

858
00:55:31,407 --> 00:55:33,711
We've gotta help these people
find the key.

859
00:55:33,755 --> 00:55:36,234
- Are you well enough to go with us?
- Go with you?

860
00:55:36,277 --> 00:55:39,495
Just tell us where that policeman
was headed and we'll take it from there.

861
00:55:39,538 --> 00:55:42,147
- Kevin, please.
- I wish I'd never seen that damn thing.

862
00:55:42,843 --> 00:55:44,843
[sighs]

863
00:55:44,886 --> 00:55:48,495
Okay, look. He said he was gonna
go to Charlie's music store, all right?

864
00:55:48,538 --> 00:55:50,625
It's at, um, Landmark Mall.

865
00:55:50,669 --> 00:55:52,278
Can you show us the way?

866
00:55:52,322 --> 00:55:53,235
- Of course.
- No.

867
00:56:03,931 --> 00:56:06,931
[Lubic] Charlie, the kid said
you know about this kind of stuff.

868
00:56:06,974 --> 00:56:08,714
You don't think
this could be Russian?

869
00:56:10,410 --> 00:56:11,366
Eh...

870
00:56:14,410 --> 00:56:16,280
[car approaches]

871
00:56:16,324 --> 00:56:17,193
[screeching]

872
00:56:24,976 --> 00:56:27,585
Well, what do you know? The
mountain comes to Muhammad.

873
00:56:32,281 --> 00:56:36,020
Hey, how come I get this feeling
I've been looking for you all night?

874
00:56:36,064 --> 00:56:38,412
I believe you have something
that belongs to us.

875
00:56:38,455 --> 00:56:41,021
- Well, let me guess. That music gizmo there?
- By the Sorceress...

876
00:56:41,065 --> 00:56:42,455
Freeze. All of you.

877
00:56:44,152 --> 00:56:47,543
Choice, really choice.
What's this, a circus act?

878
00:56:47,587 --> 00:56:49,195
Now, somebody's gonna give
me some answers around here.

879
00:56:49,239 --> 00:56:51,456
Let's start with you, blondie.

880
00:56:51,500 --> 00:56:53,240
We're not your enemies.

881
00:56:53,282 --> 00:56:55,327
If you'd just give us that, we
would be very, very grateful.

882
00:56:55,370 --> 00:56:57,674
You're not gettin' nothing
until I get some answers.

883
00:56:57,717 --> 00:57:01,196
- He-Man, He-Man. Someone's following us.
- What the hell is that?

884
00:57:01,240 --> 00:57:03,849
Neutrino Drive,
18 metrons and closing fast.

885
00:57:03,892 --> 00:57:05,718
- It's them.
- [Gwildor] At ten.

886
00:57:05,762 --> 00:57:07,501
They've locked in on the key.

887
00:57:07,544 --> 00:57:09,588
Hey. Drop your weapons or I...

888
00:57:09,631 --> 00:57:12,805
[grunts] He-Man.

889
00:57:12,849 --> 00:57:15,850
Gwildor, how long to calculate
the coordinates and take us home?

890
00:57:15,893 --> 00:57:18,415
I don't know.
The keys have all been moved.

891
00:57:18,458 --> 00:57:20,676
[chuckles] Boy,
are you people in trouble.

892
00:57:20,719 --> 00:57:23,329
He-Man, 0.61 chromons
until moonrise.

893
00:57:23,372 --> 00:57:25,503
- Teela, take these people
in the back. - Let's go.

894
00:57:25,546 --> 00:57:27,546
You can't order me around.

895
00:57:27,590 --> 00:57:30,285
Oh, if you'd rather stay and face
Evil-Lyn's commandos, that's fine with me.

896
00:57:30,329 --> 00:57:31,764
Look, believe me, sir,
you wouldn't.

897
00:57:36,677 --> 00:57:40,547
Evil-Lyn, just as
the signal indicated

898
00:57:40,591 --> 00:57:42,808
the natives and the key
are within the structure, but...

899
00:57:42,852 --> 00:57:46,287
- Yes, Karg?
- He-Man.

900
00:57:46,330 --> 00:57:50,200
The Eternians have
already arrived.

901
00:57:50,244 --> 00:57:52,895
Beastman, full-force attack
at my command.

902
00:57:52,939 --> 00:57:55,592
Karg, Blade follow me.

903
00:58:02,722 --> 00:58:03,679
How do you feel?

904
00:58:05,158 --> 00:58:06,636
I'm feeling a little hungry.

905
00:58:06,680 --> 00:58:08,288
[key beeping]

906
00:58:11,723 --> 00:58:13,593
Gwildor, you've got to hurry.

907
00:58:13,636 --> 00:58:15,897
[Gwildor] Yes, I'm working
as fast as I can.

908
00:58:15,941 --> 00:58:17,767
[key sounds chord]

909
00:58:17,810 --> 00:58:18,810
There. [clears throat]

910
00:58:20,289 --> 00:58:23,073
There's Grayskull,
and that puts us

911
00:58:24,507 --> 00:58:27,942
there, but we've to be there.

912
00:58:27,985 --> 00:58:31,638
Twenty metrons forward
if we wanna break through

913
00:58:31,682 --> 00:58:35,247
the barrier of
the Sorceress' force field.

914
00:58:35,290 --> 00:58:38,161
Wait a minute, wait a minute.
I don't understand.

915
00:58:38,204 --> 00:58:41,248
Now, what are you trying to do?

916
00:58:41,291 --> 00:58:43,856
- The universe is music, Kevin.
- [Kevin] Uh-huh.

917
00:58:43,899 --> 00:58:46,899
Hey, this is really weird, huh?

918
00:58:46,943 --> 00:58:49,204
Reminds me of
<i>Invasion of the Body Snatchers.</i>

919
00:58:49,248 --> 00:58:52,118
The part where the pods started
taking over people's bodies.

920
00:58:52,162 --> 00:58:54,379
You don't know who are pods
and who are the bodies.

921
00:58:54,423 --> 00:58:57,466
Shut up.
They're psychos, Corrigan.

922
00:58:57,510 --> 00:59:00,031
We've stumbled onto some loony
fringe group here, some kind of cult.

923
00:59:04,206 --> 00:59:05,901
Our guests are arriving.

924
00:59:09,684 --> 00:59:11,076
- [glass shattering]
- [weapons firing]

925
00:59:19,946 --> 00:59:20,685
[growls]

926
00:59:35,339 --> 00:59:36,729
[key sounding]

927
00:59:40,904 --> 00:59:42,643
- Gwildor, how much longer?
- Huh?

928
00:59:42,687 --> 00:59:45,079
I don't know. I don't know.

929
00:59:45,122 --> 00:59:47,470
I'd give all
the chalconite in Fribillian

930
00:59:47,513 --> 00:59:50,644
if I could only spend two
units with a master song maker.

931
00:59:58,297 --> 01:00:00,818
- You think they don't like us?
- No, they're just lonely.

932
01:00:00,862 --> 01:00:02,036
They miss us.

933
01:00:03,167 --> 01:00:04,167
Go.

934
01:00:28,646 --> 01:00:29,864
He-Man.

935
01:00:42,778 --> 01:00:45,474
What the hell is going on
out there, World War III?

936
01:00:45,518 --> 01:00:47,822
Hey, ain't that your buddies
getting their heads blown off?

937
01:00:50,866 --> 01:00:53,605
- Kevin, you know how to use
one of these? - Um...

938
01:00:53,648 --> 01:00:56,258
Don't let him out of sight,
and guard the key with your life.

939
01:00:56,301 --> 01:00:58,736
If anyone comes near it, you blast
him. Do you understand, Kevin?

940
01:01:08,172 --> 01:01:09,607
They're killing
each other out there.

941
01:01:13,694 --> 01:01:16,737
- Is Gwildor ready?
- Not yet. The room's secure.

942
01:01:16,781 --> 01:01:18,650
Anyway, it sounded like you
needed a woman's touch out here.

943
01:01:25,216 --> 01:01:27,912
Woman-at-Arms.

944
01:01:27,956 --> 01:01:31,304
Give me the gun, kid. Give me,
give me... Come on, give me the gun.

945
01:01:31,348 --> 01:01:33,695
Don't you get it, Lubic, huh?

946
01:01:33,738 --> 01:01:37,435
All right, this is for real.
She meant what she said.

947
01:01:37,478 --> 01:01:40,130
- I said give me the gun.
- No!

948
01:01:40,174 --> 01:01:42,913
Look, we've come this far. We're
not giving up until they get home.

949
01:01:44,522 --> 01:01:47,262
Look, don't stop,
Gwildor, all right?

950
01:01:47,305 --> 01:01:49,523
Okay, Corrigan, don't say
I didn't give you a chance.

951
01:01:49,566 --> 01:01:51,479
When this is over,
you're going to jail.

952
01:01:51,523 --> 01:01:55,132
Accessory to assault, resisting
arrest, endangering lives.

953
01:01:55,176 --> 01:02:00,914
I guarantee, you and all your buddies.
I'm gonna put you away for 850 years.

954
01:02:00,958 --> 01:02:02,089
What are you looking at, shorty?

955
01:02:04,001 --> 01:02:07,132
Mark my words, Corrigan,
you're going to jail, you hear me?

956
01:02:07,176 --> 01:02:09,306
[Kevin] Yeah, Lubic, I
hear you. Lubic, listen to me.

957
01:02:10,133 --> 01:02:10,915
Lubic...

958
01:02:20,786 --> 01:02:23,047
[Kevin] Just relax, okay?

959
01:02:23,091 --> 01:02:24,829
- All right, Gwildor, you need anything?
- Give me that thing.

960
01:02:26,134 --> 01:02:28,613
Hey. Kevin, stop it.

961
01:02:29,656 --> 01:02:31,395
[Kevin and Lubic grunting]

962
01:02:32,961 --> 01:02:34,178
[Charlie] Watch that gun.

963
01:02:34,221 --> 01:02:35,613
Come on, you're gonna get hurt.

964
01:02:38,613 --> 01:02:39,917
[both grunting]

965
01:02:53,136 --> 01:02:55,093
- Mother?
- Yes, darling, it's me.

966
01:02:56,180 --> 01:02:57,484
But the plane...

967
01:02:57,528 --> 01:03:00,441
Oh, I'm so sorry you had
to go through that, Julie,

968
01:03:00,484 --> 01:03:02,137
but we had to disappear.

969
01:03:02,181 --> 01:03:04,963
We're doing very important,
very secret work.

970
01:03:05,006 --> 01:03:06,789
Oh, honey,
I've missed you so much.

971
01:03:13,485 --> 01:03:14,703
I don't believe it.

972
01:03:15,920 --> 01:03:17,007
Mom.

973
01:03:17,877 --> 01:03:19,312
Listen, darling.

974
01:03:19,356 --> 01:03:21,486
Your new friends are tied up
with the work we're doing,

975
01:03:21,530 --> 01:03:25,312
and they have something we
want. That shiny metal thing.

976
01:03:25,356 --> 01:03:27,486
With the blinking lights.

977
01:03:27,530 --> 01:03:29,226
Will you get it for us?

978
01:03:29,270 --> 01:03:30,617
[Kevin grunting]

979
01:03:30,660 --> 01:03:31,834
Charlie!

980
01:03:33,921 --> 01:03:35,096
[Kevin] Charlie!

981
01:03:37,183 --> 01:03:38,618
[all grunting]

982
01:03:42,097 --> 01:03:44,140
[Lubic] You're a moron kid.
Watch your arm, pal...

983
01:03:44,184 --> 01:03:45,314
[gunshot]

984
01:03:48,793 --> 01:03:52,140
I don't believe it. I've got
a lot of serious work to do.

985
01:03:52,184 --> 01:03:53,314
You're acting like Torktums.

986
01:03:56,054 --> 01:03:58,272
Julie. Where's Julie?

987
01:03:58,315 --> 01:03:59,620
I...

988
01:03:59,663 --> 01:04:01,923
Kevin, you won't believe this.

989
01:04:01,967 --> 01:04:04,185
- They're alive.
- What's the matter? Where were you?

990
01:04:05,489 --> 01:04:06,750
[key beeping]

991
01:04:08,750 --> 01:04:09,881
Julie.

992
01:04:11,360 --> 01:04:12,707
Julie!

993
01:04:12,750 --> 01:04:14,490
[Gwildor] The key. The key.

994
01:04:14,534 --> 01:04:15,316
[Kevin screams]

995
01:04:21,969 --> 01:04:23,448
[Julie chuckles]

996
01:04:23,490 --> 01:04:24,838
Thank you, my darling.

997
01:04:27,187 --> 01:04:28,187
No!

998
01:04:29,752 --> 01:04:33,317
- [Kevin] Julie!
- No!

999
01:04:33,361 --> 01:04:34,491
- No.
- [Kevin] Julie.

1000
01:04:45,449 --> 01:04:46,840
[yells]

1001
01:04:49,450 --> 01:04:50,319
[He-Man] Where are they going?

1002
01:04:53,232 --> 01:04:55,014
Teela. He-Man. Hurry.

1003
01:04:57,406 --> 01:04:59,103
The key.

1004
01:04:59,146 --> 01:05:00,928
- That way.
- Bring Gwildor.

1005
01:05:01,711 --> 01:05:02,841
Hold them.

1006
01:05:04,364 --> 01:05:05,190
[Man-at-Arms] Down.

1007
01:05:12,712 --> 01:05:14,842
- [Julie] That woman took the key.
- [Man-at-Arms] Let's move.

1008
01:05:15,668 --> 01:05:16,886
[He-Man] Gwildor, come on.

1009
01:05:16,929 --> 01:05:19,756
[Gwildor] I'm going.
I'm going.

1010
01:05:23,930 --> 01:05:26,452
Charlie, you got a gun in here?

1011
01:05:26,495 --> 01:05:29,105
A gun, a gun, a gun.
For holdups.

1012
01:05:29,148 --> 01:05:30,887
In the front room,
under the counter. I got one.

1013
01:05:30,930 --> 01:05:32,453
- You got one? Go. Come on. Let's go.
- All right, all right.

1014
01:05:32,496 --> 01:05:34,279
[Lubic] Let's go.

1015
01:05:34,322 --> 01:05:38,149
Oh, my God. My store.

1016
01:05:38,192 --> 01:05:41,627
- My keyboards.
- Look at this place. Look at those guys.

1017
01:05:41,670 --> 01:05:44,844
This is an invasion.
Give me the gun.

1018
01:05:44,888 --> 01:05:46,671
- Give me the gun. Give me the gun.
- All right, all right.

1019
01:05:47,410 --> 01:05:48,541
[gun cocking]

1020
01:05:49,454 --> 01:05:50,628
Stay right there.

1021
01:05:51,454 --> 01:05:52,063
No problem.

1022
01:05:55,497 --> 01:05:56,845
Police. Nobody move.

1023
01:05:59,498 --> 01:06:00,542
[weapons firing]

1024
01:06:11,933 --> 01:06:14,064
Holy shit.

1025
01:06:14,108 --> 01:06:15,630
I think I'm gonna need
some backup.

1026
01:06:25,065 --> 01:06:27,152
Ready to transport.

1027
01:06:27,196 --> 01:06:28,761
I will send the signal
to Skeletor.

1028
01:06:35,458 --> 01:06:37,284
[key plays chords]

1029
01:06:45,980 --> 01:06:47,762
[Kevin] What's happening?

1030
01:06:47,806 --> 01:06:49,111
[He-Man] Hurry, keep moving.

1031
01:06:51,980 --> 01:06:54,459
The key.
Someone's opening a door.

1032
01:06:54,502 --> 01:06:56,763
A very big door.

1033
01:06:56,807 --> 01:06:59,068
- [He-Man] Cover your eyes.
- [Kevin] What's that?

1034
01:06:59,112 --> 01:07:01,937
- [Teela] This way, hurry.
- [Man-at-Arms] Into the alleyway, hurry.

1035
01:07:01,981 --> 01:07:04,894
- [Teela] Let's go.
- By the Sorceress. Come on.

1036
01:07:04,937 --> 01:07:08,112
It's him! It's him! [screams]

1037
01:07:29,939 --> 01:07:31,418
[dramatic music]

1038
01:07:58,290 --> 01:08:00,072
[beeping]

1039
01:08:15,726 --> 01:08:16,813
Contact Evil-Lyn.

1040
01:08:20,379 --> 01:08:22,900
[centurion] Evil-Lyn,
Skeletor demands a report.

1041
01:08:29,161 --> 01:08:31,770
I have the key, my lord.

1042
01:08:31,814 --> 01:08:36,206
The natives are fools.
Weak and easily controlled.

1043
01:08:36,249 --> 01:08:37,336
- They are...
- And He-Man?

1044
01:08:38,901 --> 01:08:41,336
- He has eluded us.
- That will be all.

1045
01:08:44,684 --> 01:08:47,250
Air Centurions, find him.

1046
01:08:54,772 --> 01:08:55,729
Come on.

1047
01:08:58,077 --> 01:09:00,469
- Hurry.
- [Teela] Air Centurions.

1048
01:09:00,512 --> 01:09:01,556
Down!

1049
01:09:12,599 --> 01:09:14,730
- Quick, he'll be back.
- All right, let's move. Come on.

1050
01:09:19,252 --> 01:09:21,557
- Come on.
- They're coming.

1051
01:09:21,600 --> 01:09:23,035
- This way.
- Hurry.

1052
01:09:23,731 --> 01:09:24,731
Come on.

1053
01:09:26,774 --> 01:09:28,123
- On the roof.
- Go, go.

1054
01:09:28,166 --> 01:09:29,774
Go! Go!

1055
01:09:36,211 --> 01:09:38,298
- They're turning around to come back.
- [He-Man] Keep moving.

1056
01:09:44,036 --> 01:09:46,080
Gwildor, your grappler,
give it to me.

1057
01:09:46,124 --> 01:09:47,080
Here, on the roof.

1058
01:09:49,212 --> 01:09:50,385
Hurry. Go.

1059
01:09:51,125 --> 01:09:51,776
Go.

1060
01:10:08,995 --> 01:10:11,256
- Where's He-Man?
- There.

1061
01:10:30,302 --> 01:10:31,518
[weapons firing]

1062
01:10:45,737 --> 01:10:47,172
No!

1063
01:10:48,346 --> 01:10:49,346
Fire.

1064
01:10:52,738 --> 01:10:54,130
He must not use that key.

1065
01:11:18,131 --> 01:11:19,261
- [weapon firing]
- [grunts]

1066
01:11:55,612 --> 01:11:57,308
[Skeletor over headset]
<i>Centurion, lead him to me.</i>

1067
01:11:59,351 --> 01:12:01,351
What do you say, Gwildor?

1068
01:12:01,395 --> 01:12:03,917
Any signal from the key?
There's got to be something.

1069
01:12:03,960 --> 01:12:05,873
Unfortunately, no.

1070
01:12:06,265 --> 01:12:07,483
Nothing.

1071
01:12:08,831 --> 01:12:11,005
He should be here by now.

1072
01:12:11,047 --> 01:12:14,352
I'm not worried about He-Man. He
knows how to take care of himself.

1073
01:12:14,396 --> 01:12:17,397
I'm more worried about getting
us out of here before they find us.

1074
01:12:17,440 --> 01:12:20,310
I only have two numbers left.

1075
01:12:20,353 --> 01:12:23,266
Once we get the key back,
we'll be gone within two pretons.

1076
01:12:24,266 --> 01:12:26,571
I think not, Gwildor.

1077
01:12:35,876 --> 01:12:39,138
Not the way to treat
your beloved ruler.

1078
01:12:40,528 --> 01:12:43,876
Throw down your weapons
or you die.

1079
01:12:56,703 --> 01:12:57,790
Gwildor,

1080
01:12:58,660 --> 01:13:01,356
you minute minion,

1081
01:13:01,400 --> 01:13:04,922
I have you to thank
for all these troubles. Why?

1082
01:13:04,965 --> 01:13:07,965
I had such grand plans for you.

1083
01:13:08,009 --> 01:13:13,270
I would never knowingly serve
the lord of Snake Mountain.

1084
01:13:13,314 --> 01:13:16,357
Wait till He-Man arrives.
He'll see to you.

1085
01:13:17,357 --> 01:13:19,184
Will he?

1086
01:13:19,227 --> 01:13:22,358
I expect him at any moment.
Take them!

1087
01:13:22,402 --> 01:13:23,141
[screams]

1088
01:13:44,794 --> 01:13:45,794
[Gwildor] Torktums.

1089
01:14:01,534 --> 01:14:04,274
He-Man, no! It's a trap!

1090
01:14:04,318 --> 01:14:05,448
[Julie screams]

1091
01:14:05,492 --> 01:14:06,492
Julie!

1092
01:14:08,231 --> 01:14:09,666
[grunts]

1093
01:14:12,014 --> 01:14:13,709
- [Julie] No.
- [Man-at-Arms] He-Man.

1094
01:14:13,753 --> 01:14:14,796
[Julie] Kevin?

1095
01:14:19,275 --> 01:14:20,841
[grunting]

1096
01:14:31,494 --> 01:14:32,797
[grunting]

1097
01:14:52,148 --> 01:14:53,930
Stay where you are, He-Man.

1098
01:14:54,973 --> 01:14:56,886
One more move,

1099
01:14:56,930 --> 01:14:59,670
and your friends will not
live to see another day.

1100
01:15:03,018 --> 01:15:03,887
It's gonna be all right.

1101
01:15:06,539 --> 01:15:08,887
I give you a choice.

1102
01:15:08,931 --> 01:15:11,931
Return with me
to Eternia as my slave,

1103
01:15:11,974 --> 01:15:14,714
and save their despicable lives,

1104
01:15:14,758 --> 01:15:18,888
or perish with them on this
primitive and tasteless planet.

1105
01:15:20,714 --> 01:15:22,584
Surrender your sword.

1106
01:15:29,672 --> 01:15:30,759
He-Man, no!

1107
01:15:32,498 --> 01:15:36,499
Teela, I have no choice.
This is our fight.

1108
01:15:36,542 --> 01:15:38,586
I don't want
innocent people to die.

1109
01:15:38,629 --> 01:15:40,238
Well said, He-Man.

1110
01:15:41,542 --> 01:15:42,586
How noble of you.

1111
01:15:48,152 --> 01:15:50,152
- Take care of them.
- Good journey.

1112
01:15:51,543 --> 01:15:52,587
Good journey.

1113
01:15:58,630 --> 01:15:59,891
What about them, sir?

1114
01:16:03,675 --> 01:16:04,935
Leave them alone.

1115
01:16:06,718 --> 01:16:08,936
He-Man is my slave.

1116
01:16:08,979 --> 01:16:11,979
As long as I let them live,
he is bound by his word.

1117
01:16:12,023 --> 01:16:13,415
Let them rot.

1118
01:16:13,457 --> 01:16:15,066
[chuckling]

1119
01:16:15,110 --> 01:16:16,371
Let them rot.

1120
01:16:24,719 --> 01:16:26,458
Let me look at her, Kevin.

1121
01:16:26,502 --> 01:16:30,111
- What's wrong with her?
- This is Skeletor's particular gift.

1122
01:16:30,155 --> 01:16:32,590
- Gwildor, we need to get back to Eternia.
- [Man-at-Arms] Immediately.

1123
01:16:32,633 --> 01:16:36,546
There's little chance of that.
The power core's melted down.

1124
01:16:36,590 --> 01:16:39,546
The tones are erased
from the key's memory.

1125
01:16:41,504 --> 01:16:43,938
There's no way home. No way.

1126
01:16:46,504 --> 01:16:48,156
[whooshing]

1127
01:17:01,331 --> 01:17:04,722
Here. Cover her
with this. Teela.

1128
01:17:05,505 --> 01:17:07,506
She's burning up.

1129
01:17:07,549 --> 01:17:10,288
We've got to get her water.
There's a fountain down below.

1130
01:17:10,332 --> 01:17:11,723
[Man-at-Arms] Good. Up.

1131
01:17:12,375 --> 01:17:13,288
[grunting]

1132
01:17:19,810 --> 01:17:21,159
[officer 1] Okay,
move out, let's go.

1133
01:17:21,202 --> 01:17:22,681
[officer 2] I'll take
the west perimeter.

1134
01:17:22,723 --> 01:17:24,855
[officer 3] Unit 3,
keep coming from there.

1135
01:17:24,897 --> 01:17:26,333
Okay, Lubic.

1136
01:17:26,376 --> 01:17:28,985
- Where's the army?
- Will you shut up!

1137
01:17:29,029 --> 01:17:30,811
They were here, I'm telling you.

1138
01:17:30,855 --> 01:17:33,594
It was the damnedest thing
you ever saw.

1139
01:17:33,637 --> 01:17:36,072
- All right, everybody, follow me.
- Let's go, guys.

1140
01:17:41,856 --> 01:17:42,943
[Man-at-Arms] Let me see this.

1141
01:17:50,335 --> 01:17:51,726
Oh, my God.

1142
01:17:59,031 --> 01:18:02,379
- What's gonna happen to her?
- The poison's already in her blood, Kevin.

1143
01:18:02,423 --> 01:18:04,858
- The wound will keep growing...
- Only our Sorceress can heal her now.

1144
01:18:05,771 --> 01:18:06,771
I'm sorry, Kevin.

1145
01:18:10,336 --> 01:18:13,424
Look, don't be sorry, just find
a way to get us back, okay?

1146
01:18:14,771 --> 01:18:16,815
I mean, there's got to be a way.

1147
01:18:18,293 --> 01:18:19,032
Isn't there?

1148
01:18:24,294 --> 01:18:25,076
Gwildor?

1149
01:18:28,207 --> 01:18:28,989
No.

1150
01:18:30,512 --> 01:18:33,076
You see, Kevin,

1151
01:18:33,120 --> 01:18:36,686
opening a dimensional door
is relatively easy.

1152
01:18:37,599 --> 01:18:38,990
But the tones, Kevin,

1153
01:18:40,426 --> 01:18:43,687
the tones that were stored
in this Cosmic Key

1154
01:18:43,730 --> 01:18:45,774
were completely erased.

1155
01:18:45,817 --> 01:18:47,774
Skeletor knew what he was doing.

1156
01:18:47,817 --> 01:18:51,556
Even if I could fix it, we could
search for a thousand years

1157
01:18:51,600 --> 01:18:54,948
and never find the tones
that will take us home.

1158
01:18:54,991 --> 01:18:57,209
But wait a minute. The tones.

1159
01:18:57,253 --> 01:18:59,862
You mean the melody the key played
every time we pressed the red button?

1160
01:19:01,383 --> 01:19:02,905
- Yeah.
- Wait a minute.

1161
01:19:04,123 --> 01:19:06,210
Wait a minute.

1162
01:19:06,254 --> 01:19:07,992
- What is it, Kevin?
- Shh.

1163
01:19:09,341 --> 01:19:11,471
[humming]

1164
01:19:11,515 --> 01:19:12,993
[instrumental music
playing over radio]

1165
01:19:13,037 --> 01:19:14,732
God, I wish that thing
would shut up.

1166
01:19:18,515 --> 01:19:21,211
Whoa. Thanks. Okay.

1167
01:19:21,255 --> 01:19:22,820
[humming]

1168
01:19:26,907 --> 01:19:30,256
[Kevin vocalizing]

1169
01:19:30,299 --> 01:19:32,560
Wait a minute, I've got it.
I've got it.

1170
01:19:33,386 --> 01:19:34,864
[whistling]

1171
01:19:38,386 --> 01:19:42,430
That's it. That's it.
How did you do that?

1172
01:19:42,473 --> 01:19:44,778
I don't know, I just... If I
hear a tune a couple of times,

1173
01:19:44,821 --> 01:19:47,039
I can usually remember it.

1174
01:19:47,082 --> 01:19:49,344
Besides, it had a good hook. I was
going to use it in one of my songs.

1175
01:19:49,387 --> 01:19:50,995
Songs?

1176
01:19:51,039 --> 01:19:53,474
Why didn't you tell me
you were a song maker?

1177
01:19:53,518 --> 01:19:57,909
Are you a master? Yes.
Yes, you are. I know that.

1178
01:19:57,953 --> 01:19:59,909
[chuckling]

1179
01:19:59,953 --> 01:20:04,475
That's why the fates brought
us here. The final chord, Kevin.

1180
01:20:04,519 --> 01:20:06,519
Twenty metrons poleward.

1181
01:20:08,128 --> 01:20:09,780
Pull it out of the air for us.

1182
01:20:16,433 --> 01:20:18,694
Look, you've got the wrong
song maker, Gwildor.

1183
01:20:18,737 --> 01:20:22,476
All right, I'm just a stupid keyboard
player in a high school band.

1184
01:20:22,520 --> 01:20:23,520
There's a million of me.

1185
01:20:27,738 --> 01:20:29,390
Only one of you, Kevin.

1186
01:20:30,651 --> 01:20:32,086
Only one of anybody.

1187
01:20:35,782 --> 01:20:37,695
Listen to me, boy.

1188
01:20:37,738 --> 01:20:39,609
In half a chromon,

1189
01:20:39,652 --> 01:20:42,652
we're not going to have
a sorceress to go home to.

1190
01:20:42,696 --> 01:20:46,000
So if you know how to do something
with that thing, then you do it.

1191
01:20:47,739 --> 01:20:50,305
Gwildor, Kevin knows the tones.

1192
01:20:50,349 --> 01:20:51,783
Can you get us home
or can't you?

1193
01:20:54,479 --> 01:20:56,479
[stammering]

1194
01:20:56,523 --> 01:20:57,784
Yes...

1195
01:20:58,740 --> 01:21:00,262
Yes, I think I can.

1196
01:21:02,827 --> 01:21:04,914
I need a few things. Hmm...

1197
01:21:04,958 --> 01:21:07,350
A bossonic tesseract.

1198
01:21:07,393 --> 01:21:10,698
- Right here.
- An octode rectifier.

1199
01:21:10,741 --> 01:21:12,133
I have an octode rectifier.

1200
01:21:12,176 --> 01:21:14,220
And something
to play the tones on.

1201
01:21:14,264 --> 01:21:15,828
Wait, I'll get a keyboard
from Charlie's.

1202
01:21:17,133 --> 01:21:19,177
- Look, take care of her.
- I will.

1203
01:21:47,570 --> 01:21:48,570
I win.

1204
01:21:52,918 --> 01:21:54,223
How long?

1205
01:21:54,267 --> 01:21:56,744
[centurion] Half a preton
until moonrise.

1206
01:21:56,788 --> 01:21:58,571
Do you hear, Sorceress?

1207
01:21:59,831 --> 01:22:02,702
The final moment has come.

1208
01:22:02,745 --> 01:22:05,310
All the forces of Grayskull,

1209
01:22:05,354 --> 01:22:09,398
all the powers of the universe
will be vested in me.

1210
01:22:09,442 --> 01:22:14,790
Me! And you will
cease to exist.

1211
01:22:14,833 --> 01:22:18,703
It is not too late
to undo this madness.

1212
01:22:18,746 --> 01:22:20,703
Madness?

1213
01:22:20,746 --> 01:22:25,920
I demand the destitution,
shame and loneliness of scorn.

1214
01:22:25,964 --> 01:22:28,704
It is my destiny.
It is my right.

1215
01:22:28,747 --> 01:22:31,486
Nothing will deter me from it.

1216
01:22:31,530 --> 01:22:34,921
Men who crave power

1217
01:22:34,965 --> 01:22:38,574
look back over the mistakes
of their lives,

1218
01:22:38,618 --> 01:22:42,966
pile them all together
and call it destiny.

1219
01:22:45,400 --> 01:22:47,227
[chuckles]

1220
01:22:47,271 --> 01:22:51,835
Thank you for that bit of philosophy,
Sorceress. Here is my response.

1221
01:22:55,619 --> 01:22:56,967
Yes, Sorceress.

1222
01:22:58,271 --> 01:22:59,185
The sword of Grayskull.

1223
01:23:01,575 --> 01:23:02,749
Mine.

1224
01:23:10,533 --> 01:23:13,011
Now and forever.

1225
01:23:18,708 --> 01:23:20,011
Your champion.

1226
01:23:31,709 --> 01:23:35,143
Witness this moment, He-Man.

1227
01:23:35,187 --> 01:23:37,491
This moment when
the powers of Grayskull

1228
01:23:37,535 --> 01:23:40,188
will become mine for eternity.

1229
01:23:40,231 --> 01:23:45,013
Our lifelong battle is ending
at last in the only way it could.

1230
01:23:45,057 --> 01:23:46,579
[centurion]
Holosphere standing by.

1231
01:23:48,013 --> 01:23:51,145
When the Great Eye opens,

1232
01:23:51,189 --> 01:23:55,623
the people of Eternia
shall see you kneeling to me

1233
01:23:55,666 --> 01:23:57,014
just before you die.

1234
01:23:58,406 --> 01:24:00,276
I'll never kneel to you!

1235
01:24:00,319 --> 01:24:03,624
Yes, you will!
Yes, you will!

1236
01:24:03,667 --> 01:24:08,233
Or I shall wreak
unforgettable harm upon you.

1237
01:24:20,016 --> 01:24:21,016
[whip snapping]

1238
01:24:29,626 --> 01:24:32,539
Lubic, let me drive you home
so you can get a little rest, huh?

1239
01:24:32,582 --> 01:24:34,148
I was in Korea.

1240
01:24:34,192 --> 01:24:35,583
I never saw anything like this.

1241
01:24:35,626 --> 01:24:36,887
[car approaching]

1242
01:24:38,627 --> 01:24:41,453
- That's him. That's him.
- [officer 1] Not again.

1243
01:24:41,496 --> 01:24:43,540
- [officer 2] Come on, Lubic.
- Come on, we're moving in.

1244
01:24:48,410 --> 01:24:50,018
[car approaching]

1245
01:24:58,150 --> 01:24:59,889
I got it.

1246
01:24:59,932 --> 01:25:02,237
- How is she?
- The same, Kevin.

1247
01:25:02,281 --> 01:25:04,368
Okay, this should give us
the tones we need.

1248
01:25:04,411 --> 01:25:06,194
How?

1249
01:25:06,237 --> 01:25:07,368
Just press the keys.

1250
01:25:07,411 --> 01:25:09,759
Keys? What keys?

1251
01:25:10,803 --> 01:25:11,933
Oh, no, no, no. Here.

1252
01:25:11,977 --> 01:25:12,933
- [strikes keys]
- Ah!

1253
01:25:16,759 --> 01:25:17,933
Excellent.

1254
01:25:17,977 --> 01:25:19,195
[chuckles]

1255
01:25:20,282 --> 01:25:21,934
[groaning]

1256
01:25:21,978 --> 01:25:23,325
[Gwildor playing keyboard]

1257
01:25:24,369 --> 01:25:26,630
Wonderful.

1258
01:25:26,673 --> 01:25:29,891
You never told me you
had sonic keys in this world.

1259
01:25:29,934 --> 01:25:31,283
I just hope it helps, Gwildor.

1260
01:25:31,326 --> 01:25:32,935
- Thank you, Kevin.
- It's okay.

1261
01:25:37,979 --> 01:25:39,979
I'll have this ready
in a preton.

1262
01:25:42,022 --> 01:25:43,979
Kevin, please don't leave me.

1263
01:25:46,022 --> 01:25:47,284
I promise you, Julie,

1264
01:25:49,588 --> 01:25:50,936
I'll never leave you.

1265
01:25:52,632 --> 01:25:53,632
Never.

1266
01:26:00,372 --> 01:26:01,546
I love you.

1267
01:26:04,546 --> 01:26:05,763
I love you.

1268
01:26:08,199 --> 01:26:09,416
- [whip snapping]
- [grunting]

1269
01:26:13,721 --> 01:26:14,721
Enough.

1270
01:26:17,677 --> 01:26:19,808
Where is your strength?

1271
01:26:19,851 --> 01:26:21,851
Where has it gone, huh?

1272
01:26:21,895 --> 01:26:23,809
Look at your precious Sorceress.

1273
01:26:23,851 --> 01:26:26,809
An old crone.
Weak. Withering.

1274
01:26:27,504 --> 01:26:28,765
Dying.

1275
01:26:30,504 --> 01:26:33,026
Are you ready to kneel now,

1276
01:26:33,070 --> 01:26:35,244
proud warrior?

1277
01:26:35,288 --> 01:26:37,201
The moon rises to its apex.

1278
01:26:37,244 --> 01:26:38,201
Ah.

1279
01:26:40,766 --> 01:26:42,375
Do you hear?

1280
01:26:42,418 --> 01:26:43,202
Huh?

1281
01:26:45,419 --> 01:26:48,810
The alpha and the omega.

1282
01:26:48,853 --> 01:26:50,811
Death and rebirth,

1283
01:26:51,593 --> 01:26:53,941
and as you die,

1284
01:26:55,028 --> 01:26:59,767
so will I be reborn.

1285
01:27:10,073 --> 01:27:12,029
What are they doing over there?

1286
01:27:12,073 --> 01:27:13,638
We've gotta stop this fast.

1287
01:27:13,681 --> 01:27:14,768
- Okay.
- No.

1288
01:27:16,116 --> 01:27:18,508
Stay here and cover me.
Spread out.

1289
01:27:18,552 --> 01:27:20,030
- And wait for my signal.
- Yes, sir.

1290
01:27:21,552 --> 01:27:22,943
These guys are mine.

1291
01:27:26,205 --> 01:27:29,030
<i>People of Eternia.</i>

1292
01:27:29,074 --> 01:27:33,770
<i>I stand before the Great Eye
of the Galaxy</i>

1293
01:27:33,814 --> 01:27:36,553
<i>chosen by destiny</i>

1294
01:27:36,596 --> 01:27:40,162
<i>to receive the powers
of Grayskull.</i>

1295
01:27:40,206 --> 01:27:41,770
This inevitable moment

1296
01:27:41,814 --> 01:27:44,510
will transpire before your eyes

1297
01:27:44,554 --> 01:27:48,641
even as He-Man himself
bears witness to it.

1298
01:27:48,684 --> 01:27:50,032
[centurion] The Eye opens.

1299
01:27:50,076 --> 01:27:53,989
Now, I, Skeletor,

1300
01:27:55,381 --> 01:27:58,294
am Master of the Universe.

1301
01:28:01,250 --> 01:28:02,251
Yes!

1302
01:28:14,512 --> 01:28:15,947
[whooshing]

1303
01:28:18,686 --> 01:28:19,860
Yes.

1304
01:28:20,773 --> 01:28:21,817
I feel it.

1305
01:28:23,557 --> 01:28:26,209
The power fills me.

1306
01:28:27,296 --> 01:28:29,210
Yes.

1307
01:28:29,253 --> 01:28:32,992
I feel the universe within me.

1308
01:28:33,035 --> 01:28:37,384
I am... I am a part
of the cosmos.

1309
01:28:37,427 --> 01:28:39,340
Its energy flows,

1310
01:28:39,384 --> 01:28:40,819
flows through me.

1311
01:28:44,819 --> 01:28:47,123
Of what consequence are you now?

1312
01:28:47,167 --> 01:28:49,602
This planet, these people,

1313
01:28:49,646 --> 01:28:53,733
they are nothing to me.
The universe is power.

1314
01:28:54,602 --> 01:28:58,168
Pure, unstoppable power.

1315
01:28:58,212 --> 01:29:01,560
And I am that force!
I am that power!

1316
01:29:03,864 --> 01:29:06,212
Kneel before your master!

1317
01:29:08,516 --> 01:29:09,516
Fool.

1318
01:29:10,777 --> 01:29:12,908
You are no longer my equal.

1319
01:29:14,213 --> 01:29:16,691
I am more than man.

1320
01:29:16,735 --> 01:29:18,474
More than life.

1321
01:29:19,256 --> 01:29:20,735
I am

1322
01:29:21,387 --> 01:29:23,126
a God!

1323
01:29:24,083 --> 01:29:24,952
[thunder rumbling]

1324
01:29:36,432 --> 01:29:37,910
[Skeletor yelling]

1325
01:29:45,345 --> 01:29:46,389
Now,

1326
01:29:47,563 --> 01:29:49,911
you will

1327
01:29:49,954 --> 01:29:51,564
kneel!

1328
01:29:51,607 --> 01:29:52,954
[grunts]

1329
01:29:54,216 --> 01:29:55,172
Kneel!

1330
01:29:57,694 --> 01:29:58,781
Are you ready, Kevin?

1331
01:29:59,564 --> 01:30:01,086
[sighs] Yeah.

1332
01:30:01,129 --> 01:30:03,086
I'm going to set the power.
Now, here goes.

1333
01:30:07,782 --> 01:30:09,434
[electrical buzzing]

1334
01:30:10,521 --> 01:30:12,521
Now, Kevin, now!

1335
01:30:14,174 --> 01:30:16,043
[playing chords]

1336
01:30:22,043 --> 01:30:25,392
Freeze! Nobody move.
You're all under arrest.

1337
01:30:25,435 --> 01:30:28,001
Throw down your weapons and
place your hands on your heads.

1338
01:30:28,044 --> 01:30:31,393
- You have the right to remain silent...
- Lubic, you don't understand.

1339
01:30:31,436 --> 01:30:34,219
- We've gotta get back.
- Nobody's going anywhere!

1340
01:30:34,262 --> 01:30:35,697
[all yelling]

1341
01:30:40,654 --> 01:30:42,002
Where are they?

1342
01:30:43,481 --> 01:30:45,784
Where are your friends now?

1343
01:30:47,481 --> 01:30:51,872
Tell me about
the loneliness of good, He-Man.

1344
01:30:51,916 --> 01:30:56,742
Is it equal to
the loneliness of evil, huh?

1345
01:30:56,785 --> 01:30:58,656
[electrical buzzing]

1346
01:30:58,699 --> 01:31:00,046
[thunder rumbling]

1347
01:31:20,396 --> 01:31:23,179
- Holy shit.
- We did it.

1348
01:31:23,223 --> 01:31:25,135
- Gwildor, get down.
- Destroy them!

1349
01:31:26,484 --> 01:31:27,658
Take cover!

1350
01:31:36,267 --> 01:31:37,832
You promised not to hurt them.

1351
01:31:37,875 --> 01:31:38,875
I lied.

1352
01:31:39,659 --> 01:31:42,007
Farewell, He-Man.

1353
01:31:44,441 --> 01:31:45,920
Block him!

1354
01:31:45,963 --> 01:31:47,007
He-Man, quick.

1355
01:31:48,833 --> 01:31:50,746
Get him!

1356
01:31:50,789 --> 01:31:53,399
Give He-Man some cover action.
Kevin, watch the rear.

1357
01:31:53,442 --> 01:31:56,051
You.
Watch the forward position.

1358
01:31:56,095 --> 01:31:59,182
Will somebody tell me what
the hell's going on around here?

1359
01:31:59,226 --> 01:32:01,226
I feel like I'm in <i>The
Twilight Zone</i> or something.

1360
01:32:01,269 --> 01:32:03,877
Lubic, this is for real,
all right? Just get down.

1361
01:32:05,835 --> 01:32:09,965
Hey. Nobody takes
pot-shots at Lubic.

1362
01:32:10,009 --> 01:32:12,878
All right, pinkos, you wanna
play games? Then let's play.

1363
01:32:16,618 --> 01:32:17,835
Come on, you mother...

1364
01:32:25,010 --> 01:32:26,792
[grunting]

1365
01:32:26,836 --> 01:32:28,966
[Skeletor] No. Don't kill him.
I want him alive.

1366
01:32:48,794 --> 01:32:49,838
[grunting]

1367
01:33:19,232 --> 01:33:21,449
You cannot hide from me.

1368
01:33:21,493 --> 01:33:23,057
[laughing maniacally]

1369
01:33:43,320 --> 01:33:44,668
[rumbling]

1370
01:33:49,234 --> 01:33:50,756
Karg, prepare
the battle station.

1371
01:33:50,799 --> 01:33:52,799
Surely you won't leave
with Skeletor still...

1372
01:33:53,886 --> 01:33:56,582
Yeah. Warlord, let's go.

1373
01:33:58,278 --> 01:33:59,235
Signal the retreat.

1374
01:34:09,626 --> 01:34:11,061
No!

1375
01:34:20,453 --> 01:34:23,366
I have the power!

1376
01:34:27,411 --> 01:34:29,237
You.

1377
01:34:29,280 --> 01:34:33,541
You will no longer stand
between me and my destiny.

1378
01:34:33,585 --> 01:34:37,367
But I will. I told you
it was always between us.

1379
01:34:37,411 --> 01:34:41,673
Oh, I ache to smash you
out of existence.

1380
01:34:41,715 --> 01:34:45,368
To drive your cursed face
from my memory forever.

1381
01:34:45,412 --> 01:34:50,239
- Enough talk.
- Yes. Let this be our final battle.

1382
01:34:56,630 --> 01:34:57,761
[weapons clanging]

1383
01:35:36,807 --> 01:35:38,807
[screams]

1384
01:35:48,243 --> 01:35:49,243
Skeletor.

1385
01:35:50,112 --> 01:35:51,504
[panting]

1386
01:35:53,808 --> 01:35:56,026
- It's over.
- Yes.

1387
01:35:59,069 --> 01:36:00,026
For you.

1388
01:36:06,635 --> 01:36:07,679
[grunts]

1389
01:36:14,027 --> 01:36:16,070
[screams]

1390
01:36:19,028 --> 01:36:23,767
No! [screams] No!

1391
01:36:28,071 --> 01:36:29,028
[door opens]

1392
01:36:38,855 --> 01:36:41,942
He did it. He-Man!

1393
01:36:41,985 --> 01:36:44,029
- Victory!
- Victory!

1394
01:36:48,638 --> 01:36:49,812
[sighs]

1395
01:36:52,943 --> 01:36:53,986
Victory.

1396
01:36:56,683 --> 01:36:58,987
Well, Lubic, look at you.

1397
01:36:59,031 --> 01:37:01,205
Ha! So you're really
gonna stay here, huh?

1398
01:37:01,249 --> 01:37:03,423
What, are you kidding? What
am I gonna go back there for?

1399
01:37:03,465 --> 01:37:06,597
And look what I got here.
I got... I got a castle.

1400
01:37:06,640 --> 01:37:09,771
I got a view, I got clean air,
I got a beautiful woman. Huh?

1401
01:37:11,858 --> 01:37:13,379
Some kind of retirement, huh?
[chuckles]

1402
01:37:20,032 --> 01:37:24,685
Julie, keep this with you and
Eternia will always be near.

1403
01:37:28,424 --> 01:37:29,381
[Julie] Thank you.

1404
01:37:30,425 --> 01:37:32,251
[exhales]

1405
01:37:32,294 --> 01:37:33,642
I guess this is really
goodbye, huh?

1406
01:37:35,860 --> 01:37:36,947
He-Man,

1407
01:37:37,903 --> 01:37:39,860
Teela, Man-at-Arms.

1408
01:37:39,903 --> 01:37:41,947
Don't. Don't say goodbye.

1409
01:37:44,382 --> 01:37:45,382
Say, "Good journey."

1410
01:37:48,600 --> 01:37:50,077
There's an old Eternian saying,

1411
01:37:51,600 --> 01:37:53,252
"Live the journey

1412
01:37:53,295 --> 01:37:55,426
for every destination
is but a doorway to another."

1413
01:37:57,643 --> 01:37:58,427
Good journey.

1414
01:38:02,688 --> 01:38:03,905
Good journey. [chuckles]

1415
01:38:12,341 --> 01:38:13,428
Take care, Julie.

1416
01:38:15,819 --> 01:38:18,297
- You look after her, now.
- I will.

1417
01:38:18,341 --> 01:38:20,298
Activate the doorway, Gwildor.

1418
01:38:20,341 --> 01:38:25,080
Uh, are you sure, uh, you don't
wanna go back in your planet's history?

1419
01:38:25,124 --> 01:38:27,733
I could take you back in time
to the past or future.

1420
01:38:27,777 --> 01:38:30,167
No, no, look, Gwildor, that's
okay. Just send us home.

1421
01:38:30,211 --> 01:38:31,646
We better get home, Gwildor.

1422
01:38:32,646 --> 01:38:33,994
[playing notes on key]

1423
01:38:35,472 --> 01:38:36,690
[thunder rumbling]

1424
01:38:46,952 --> 01:38:50,995
- Good journey, Julie.
- Good journey, Gwildor.

1425
01:38:51,039 --> 01:38:52,865
[giggling]

1426
01:38:57,387 --> 01:38:58,692
Good journey.

1427
01:39:00,648 --> 01:39:02,214
[triumphant music]

1428
01:39:07,996 --> 01:39:09,475
Gwildor. Wait. Send us back...

1429
01:39:18,476 --> 01:39:19,694
[gasps]

1430
01:39:22,694 --> 01:39:24,563
[dog barking]

1431
01:39:24,607 --> 01:39:25,911
[birds chirping]

1432
01:39:56,218 --> 01:39:58,044
Mom, Dad, hi.

1433
01:39:58,087 --> 01:40:00,044
- You're up bright and early.
- You're all right.

1434
01:40:00,087 --> 01:40:02,349
[chuckles] Hey,
what's this all about?

1435
01:40:02,392 --> 01:40:05,479
I love you both so much.
I don't ever want to lose you.

1436
01:40:05,523 --> 01:40:07,871
We're just going away for
the day. We'll be back tonight.

1437
01:40:07,914 --> 01:40:09,784
No.

1438
01:40:09,827 --> 01:40:13,001
I changed my mind. I do wanna
go to the beach with you today.

1439
01:40:13,045 --> 01:40:14,785
Don't go to Catalina, okay?

1440
01:40:14,828 --> 01:40:18,089
- Don't be silly, honey. Stay home
and study. - Mom, Dad, please.

1441
01:40:19,654 --> 01:40:20,959
Don't get on that plane today.

1442
01:40:22,394 --> 01:40:24,264
I have a terrible feeling.

1443
01:40:24,307 --> 01:40:27,264
But Julie, your father's an
excellent pilot. It's a short trip.

1444
01:40:27,307 --> 01:40:28,046
No.

1445
01:40:30,742 --> 01:40:34,699
- Julie. Julie, put those keys back.
- I love you.

1446
01:40:34,742 --> 01:40:37,090
Julie, where are you going?
Come back here.

1447
01:40:40,874 --> 01:40:43,004
- [Kevin] Julie.
- Kevin.

1448
01:40:47,917 --> 01:40:50,091
[Kevin] Oh. Oh...

1449
01:40:50,135 --> 01:40:53,048
- Don't let your parents get on that plane.
- I've already stopped them.

1450
01:40:54,701 --> 01:40:55,875
Wait a minute.

1451
01:40:57,005 --> 01:40:58,005
You know?

1452
01:40:59,440 --> 01:41:00,223
Yeah.

1453
01:41:01,441 --> 01:41:02,267
We were there.

1454
01:41:08,441 --> 01:41:09,223
Eternia.

1455
01:41:15,832 --> 01:41:17,398
[instrumental music]

1456
01:41:20,485 --> 01:41:24,007
I have the power!

1457
01:41:26,443 --> 01:41:28,225
[theme music playing]

1458
01:45:29,417 --> 01:45:30,461
I'll be back.